ttle people can reach. So you are required and you can do magic. \r\nYou have one life and you thankfully got your gift for it. \r\nYou have not to be arrogant in order not to lose work and people \r\nThere is always a link between digital marketing and web + mobile development\r\nPeople we are targeting are people who do not have a website and people who have but need improvement or totally change to website and that make a plenty of work opportunities\r\nDepend on long term relationships and be part of your client business. Do not create websites only and leave them. Get more business out of them.\r\nRepetitive follow up is the key to getting a deal. You have to be insistive.\r\nFreelancers are many and clients are many also what make us get more clients is good marketing, follow up and good dealing\r\nBusiness is a big cycle that is built on two factors: freelancers and clients. These two factors will last forever. So, do not worry and learn how to hook your clients and understand the business cycle.  \r\nFollow your team work from mobile using the GitHub app.\r\nGet your team commits on dashboard and apply them to all other dashboards \r\nBeing accurate in your deadlines and work requirements is the key to always being required from clients.\r\nWhat makes Boula successful in freelance business are: help of god, mentality, references, set of knowledge and experience and automation website\r\nMake online business and study your only choice.	\r\nTake part of website cost to guarantee the client seriousity \r\nDo not give access to source code to clients until you get paid the full website cost\r\nAlways use google drive for mobile and google desktop to sync files in mobile and pc\r\nAlways care about cross devices files (Mean those google drive word documents that can be accessed and modified from mobile and pc at the same time)\r\nDepend on templates for website and react native mobile apps\r\nUse timer for short term actions \r\nBe active in following up your clients because clients come with insisting and getting updates.\r\nAlways open your whatsapp two accounts on laptop\r\nBe friendly with clients and always follow up them and share celebrations to their Eids and festivals with them\r\nMake Ibrahim do the embarrassing calls with clients\r\nIf you want to record a video or entered and interview with clients use virtual background to avoid being in not suitable place\r\nAdd freelancer to a page on your notebook yellow light app and start writing freelance name and tasks they have to do to send them easily from mobile to whatsapp\r\nMake boundaries a stair to summit\r\nDo not link yourself with a must to attend courses and always take online courses with certificates\r\nYou must take 25% of project cost before starting \r\nYou must be a long life support for your clients and you must also make them feel that they trust you and feel safe about their digital business. Do not be just a freelancer who did them a task and disappeared  \r\nPut a paper with all the projects you received since your start on a wall beside you in your working room to be in front of you all the time \r\nDo not receive or even be bridged in projects and tasks that require technologies you do not know because that may put you in trouble with customers \r\n\r\n\r\nDanger lines \r\nThere are two lines in a mobile home that consists of 8 apps whatsapp,  whatsapp business, messenger, and freelance references for the first line and facebook,linkedin,gmail and messages for the second line. It is a must in my business journey \r\n\r\nWhat is next?\r\n-web development\r\n-WordPress development\r\n-mobile development + laravel to your freelance\r\n-Google Marketing\r\n-Social Marketing\r\n-Graduation projects\r\n-Website or mopile system mangement and content creator\r\n-youtube channel\r\n-online courses zoom or udemy\r\n-create your own ecommerce website to pay laptops and pcs \r\n-open computer maintenance shop\r\n-add mobile maintenance to your shop\r\n-Add PlayStation 4 games and seal with accessories\r\nBig goal\r\nMy big goal is creating advertisement company that stands on three main categories\r\n1- Marketing (Google and Social)\r\n2- Website\r\n3- Mobile app\r\nAnd make it taqseet aqsat\r\n\r\nMust be achieved goal \r\nI need to reach a point where I am a social marketer and google marketer expert and I am the one who deals with clients while my programmers team do tasks and I supervise them.Also I work on programming tasks when urgent.\r\n\r\nMy Approved technologies\r\nWeb Front: Angular, React and HTML Bootstrap\r\nWeb Back: Laravel and php native\r\nMobile: React Native\r\nWordPress\r\n\r\nCompetitors\r\n\r\nhttps://www.facebook.com/100085919770060/posts/pfbid02sMyXEDf9RxdpiYA8sz85YzpKT3GSga1EPBNLJR3CzaLjK6ac2wvCQXcB3WxfgA4ul/?mibextid=Nif5oz\r\n\r\nServer\r\nStart Date : July 2023\r\nEnd Date: July 2026\r\n\r\nBest and most comfortable work position\r\nIt is when combine a desk or table and coach together and sleep under desk and start working. Something like launch tables in hospitals and also something like your father machine and coach. Note desk show have big part without any legs to cover the coach \r\n\r\nHow to calculate task cost \r\n1- cal expected time in hours\r\n2- multiply in hour cost 100\r\n\r\nNo jobless time methodology\r\nWhile working on websites try to get new tasks to start doing them after current tasks is done \r\n\r\nTime management methodology\r\n\r\n1- at the beginning of your work day choose projects that you will work\r\n2- determine time you will work for each project according to your working hours \r\n3- set timer for that and do not take rest except in breaks between projects\r\n\r\nRecovery Key for hostgator account\r\n47a306e3-d317-39a2-a096-e5af0202b216\r\n\r\nIncrease work productivity methodology(The most important)\r\n\r\nUsage: organize and accelerate work plus increase productivity\r\n1- divide all work day into tasks using pen and paper \r\n2- use Todo Tree vscode extension\r\n3- make someone tell you the tasks one by one while you are adding them using tree todo extension and writing who will do what for each task \r\n4- to add tasks quickly copy <Todo (boula)> and change it accordingly to avoid using alt+shift+f\r\n5- if you found any additional while working add them directly\r\n6- Ask your team to add tasks directly once they found them while testing or even while coding \r\n7- after adding all tasks search for all of them using ctrl+shift+f and write easy in tasks that will not take much time to finish them first after that do this process again and again until finishing all of them\r\n\r\nNote: This methodology must be always used and if extension became unavailable use similar tools especially those which will link task with start code and file\r\n\r\nNote: writing tasks inside code is severely important to reach them easily and update them with team using git and also to use git advantages with tasks like return to deleted tasks when needed\r\n\r\nNote: when meeting clients you must take notes using pen and paper to be able to apply this methodology\r\n\r\nNote: if todo tree vscode extension was not available, find tasks using ctrl + shift + f  to search for them and lust them in search results\r\n\r\nPerform them according to difficulty\r\n\r\nNote: use with this methodology the multiple project methodology\r\n\r\nMultiple project methodology\r\nUsage: working on many project at the same time \r\n1- open three desktop tabs and for each tab open a project and run it on chrome \r\n2- using increase working productivity methodology start working on them together \r\n\r\nStart working day methodology\r\nUsage Save time by starting the working day with opening a desktop for each project I will work on and add the following to it \r\n1-	vscode project\r\n2-	remote terminal with cd project\r\n3-	serve website on google\r\n4-	terminal database\r\n\r\nBest working mode methodology\r\n1-	Work on a table that help you to be under it completely and put your computer books on it \r\n2-	Listen to music on laptop using mobile speakers by the soundwire desktop app and add the player to a seprate desktop to prevent it from distracting you while moving through tabs  and use keyboard music player keys to control songs\r\nAvoiding short time client methodology\r\nIt is used when client require many ajustments within a very short period of time, and it is applied by reaching all the requirments even If the code structure and logic is not correct. This is very good to make the client trust you and give you money\r\nSpeech tasks methodology (Important)\r\nI use a text to speech app as my task manager to easily listen to tasks in a pdf or word. And I go to recent in the app to get the latest updates I did on tasks. And use timer to keep watching time while working \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nAnti Procrastination methodology\r\n1-	Set timer for the continuous period you are going work and do not break it except for toilet\r\n2-	Do not use facebook or any distribution source during this period\r\n3-	After finishing work period set time to break period\r\n4-	Break and Work periods are determined according to following calculations\r\n8 AM work\r\n10 AM Break\r\n11 Am Work\r\n1 Pm Break\r\n2 Am work\r\n4 pm Break\r\n5 pm Work\r\n\r\n7 pm break\r\n9 pm work \r\n11 pm break\r\n12 Am work\r\n2 Am brek\r\n3 Am Work\r\n5 Am break\r\n6 Am work\r\n7 Am break\r\n5-	Set all these alarms on pc and work alarms on mobile since in break period you will not be near the pc\r\n6-	If you are waking up in work periods you have to start immediately and have breakfast and coffee in nex brek period\r\nWork office methodology \r\n1- use big screen either with your laptop or with a case and if with laptop set display resolution and dimension and settings to fit the big screen size \r\n2- use medical chair with wheels \r\n3- use suitable disk \r\n4- use mouse and keyboard \r\n5-	Do not allow anybody to share network with you \r\n6-	Set dimensions and resolutions as you like in general\r\nPassive income sources\r\nIt is very important to have passive income\r\n1-Bank certificates\r\n2- Flat rent \r\n3- e-commerce websites commision \r\n\r\nLockScreen tasks image methodology\r\nVery important to have your daily tasks on your mobile lockscreen not to forget your tasks \r\nKeys of success\r\n1-	Using Project Mangement refrence and how to deal with manging tasks\r\n2-	Mangement skilld save time and effort and give success \r\n3-	I want to shift to project mangement career as a freelancer\r\n4-	LockScreen tasks image methodology\r\n5-	Automation website\r\n\r\nAdding tasks to desktop sticky notes app methodology\r\nAdding tasks using desktop	 app while sharing screen with clients \r\n\r\nSleeping and using keyboard only methodology\r\nSleeping and put laptop on a table on my side to easily work and try not to miss this methodology since it is very important\r\n\r\nSet team and divide tasks before your nap methodology \r\nIf you are going to sleep or travel or rake break give your team the required tasks to prevent wasting time \r\n\r\nTask management methodology \r\nDivide tasks according to its difficulty level\r\nStart from easy to difficult until you finish them \r\n\r\nSS methodology \r\nSS ->Standing and Sleeping positions \r\nI have to work while standing and also work while sleeping and stop working while seating because it is very boring \r\nWork while standing if task is difficult\r\n\r\nBig Note\r\nDo not kill Yousab Tech and continue as two companies and let ibrahim manage yousab and you manage Elmotahda\r\n\r\n\r\nMarketing team roles\r\nCreate facebook ads\r\nReply to unsubscribed clients\r\nReply to subscribed clients and link them to developers\r\n\r\n\r\ncontract Methodology\r\nContact between elmotahda and the client indicate when a group of features will be done and what cost is required. These milestones will depend on the project complexity and features. In case of any new tasks will be for additional time and additional cost and will be added to contact as an update.\r\nClient and Company have to be strict to the contract items\r\n\r\n\r\nPowered by Etida  none egyption pound\r\nChalnges meet the clients \r\nDeadline missing \r\nConnection\r\nLack of Commitment \r\nQuality Control\r\nLicking ibfotmation\r\nMisunderstanding reqs on time frame and Budget effection on that\r\nInteruptions of not expected conditions\r\nInsifficent onfo lead to wrong outcome\r\n\r\nPayment methodology fixed princible \r\nWe have to take 50% of cost as down payment \r\n\r\nFreelance important skills\r\nCommunucation skills\r\nTime mangement\r\nSelf discpline or motivayion\r\nNegotiatio\r\nProject mangement\r\n\r\n\r\nCommunication skills\r\nTechnical inteligance 20%\r\nEmotionql inteligence 80%\r\nGood listner + summaroze client reqs\n\n\n\nYousab problems\n1- Having skills and experience mixed with laziness in you and lack of it with your team \r\n2- ability to do easy tasks only in your team \r\n3- No existence for effective Marketing\n4- Targetting egyption market instead of saudi market\n5- Takiing too much of work on yourself without taking ibrahim to help you by runing and debuging\n\n\n\n\nYpysab pro max\nkermina finish design ibrahim finish api you link them to complete the  project\r\n\r\n20k minimum projects cost\r\n\r\nyou have to manage two parts Team and Clients\r\n\r\nUse stable code of react post and get\r\n\r\nUse database in carts and favourite or similar mattrs\r\n\r\nUse workspace create modules to avoid errors \r\n\r\nAdd videos to show how to go through these things and put your hand out of technical things \r\n\r\n\r\nWork only on react laravel projects\n\nNo free hosting\nNo google ads\nNo wordpress\r\nNo multi lang\n\n\nWork Smart\n\n\n1- for react & reactnative projects\r\nFirst create all backend \r\nSecond create all front design \r\nThird link them by giving a file that has api url  + api response + react component foreach conponent \r\n\r\n2- for fullstack laravel project\r\n First create all backend \r\nSecond create all front design \r\nThird link them by giving a databae tables contents + laravel component foreach conponent \r\n\r\n\r\n3- for wordpeess take it for programmers\r\n\r\nNote: You only have the role of project mangement and linking back with front through api do not got to any other parts\r\nNote: you may use a template for design if needed\r\nNote: this way helps you to accelrate backend and frontend work as soon as possible\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nEXAMPLE\r\nimport React, { useState, useEffect } from \"react\";\r\nimport axios from \"axios\";\r\nimport { useNavigate } from \"react-router-dom\";\r\nimport {\r\n  Container,\r\n  Row,\r\n  Col,\r\n  Card,\r\n  Button,\r\n  ListGroup,\r\n  Table,\r\n  Form,\r\n  Spinner\r\n} from \"react-bootstrap\";\r\nimport \"bootstrap/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css\";\r\n\r\nconst Profile = () => {\r\n  const [activeTab, setActiveTab] = useState(\"dashboard\");\r\n  const [orders, setOrders] = useState([]);\r\n  const [loadingOrders, setLoadingOrders] = useState(false);\r\n  const [isLoggedIn, setIsLoggedIn] = useState(!!localStorage.getItem(\"token\"));\r\n  const [cartItems, setCartItems] = useState([]);\r\n  const [user, setUser] = useState(null);\r\n  const [loadingProfile, setLoadingProfile] = useState(true);\r\n  const navigate = useNavigate();\r\n\r\n  useEffect(() => {\r\n    setIsLoggedIn(!!localStorage.getItem(\"token\"));\r\n    if (isLoggedIn) {\r\n      fetchUserProfile();\r\n      fetchCartItems();\r\n    }\r\n  }, [isLoggedIn]);\r\n\r\n  const fetchUserProfile = async () => {\r\n    const token = localStorage.getItem(\"token\");\r\n    if (!token) return;\r\n\r\n    try {\r\n      const response = await fetch(\"https://yousab-tech.com/Florifliwer/public/api/auth/user-profile\", {\r\n        headers: {\r\n          Authorization: `Bearer ${token}`,\r\n          Accept: \"application/json\"\r\n        }\r\n      });\r\n      const data = await response.json();\r\n      setUser(data);\r\n    } catch (error) {\r\n      console.error(\"Error fetching user profile:\", error);\r\n    } finally {\r\n      setLoadingProfile(false);\r\n    }\r\n  };\r\n\r\n  const fetchCartItems = async () => {\r\n    const token = localStorage.getItem(\"token\");\r\n    if (!token) return;\r\n\r\n    try {\r\n      const response = await fetch(\"https://yousab-tech.com/Florifliwer/public/api/auth/cart\", {\r\n        method: \"GET\",\r\n        headers: {\r\n          \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\",\r\n          Authorization: `Bearer ${token}`\r\n        },\r\n      });\r\n\r\n      const data = await response.json();\r\n      if (data.cart) {\r\n        setCartItems(data.cart);\r\n      }\r\n    } catch (error) {\r\n      console.error(\"Error fetching cart items:\", error);\r\n    }\r\n  };\r\n\r\n  const handleLogout = () => {\r\n    localStorage.removeItem(\"token\");\r\n    setIsLoggedIn(false);\r\n    setCartItems([]);\r\n    navigate(\"/\");\r\n    window.location.reload();\r\n  };\r\n\r\n  useEffect(() => {\r\n    if (activeTab === \"orders\") {\r\n      fetchOrders();\r\n    }\r\n  }, [activeTab]);\r\n\r\n  const fetchOrders = async () => {\r\n    try {\r\n      setLoadingOrders(true);\r\n      const token = localStorage.getItem(\"token\");\r\n\r\n      const res = await axios.get(\r\n        \"https://yousab-tech.com/Florifliwer/public/api/auth/orders?per_page=5\",\r\n        {\r\n          headers: {\r\n            Authorization: `Bearer ${token}`,\r\n            Accept: \"application/json\"\r\n          }\r\n        }\r\n      );\r\n\r\n      setOrders(res.data.data);\r\n    } catch (error) {\r\n      console.error(\"Failed to fetch orders:\", error);\r\n    } finally {\r\n      setLoadingOrders(false);\r\n    }\r\n  };\r\n\r\n  if (loadingProfile) {\r\n    return (\r\n      <Container className=\"text-center py-5\">\r\n        <Spinner animation=\"border\" />\r\n      </Container>\r\n    );\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  return (\r\n    <Container className=\"my-4\">\r\n      <h2 className=\"text-center\">Profile</h2>\r\n      <p className=\"text-center text-muted\">\r\n        <a href=\"/\" className=\"breadlink\">Home</a> / Profile\r\n      </p>\r\n      <Row>\r\n        <Col md={3}>\r\n          <Card>\r\n            <Card.Body className=\"text-center\">\r\n              <div className=\"mb-3\">\r\n                <img\r\n                  src={user?.image || \"https://via.placeholder.com/100\"}\r\n                  alt=\"Profile\"\r\n                  className=\"rounded-circle\"\r\n                  style={{ height: \"100px\" }}\r\n                />\r\n              </div>\r\n              <Card.Title>{user?.fullname || \"User\"}</Card.Title>\r\n              <Card.Text>{user?.email || \"example@mail.com\"}</Card.Text>\r\n              <ListGroup variant=\"flush\">\r\n                <ListGroup.Item\r\n                  active={activeTab === \"dashboard\"}\r\n                  onClick={() => setActiveTab(\"dashboard\")}\r\n                  action\r\n                >\r\n                  Dashboard\r\n                </ListGroup.Item>\r\n                <ListGroup.Item\r\n                  active={activeTab === \"orders\"}\r\n                  onClick={() => setActiveTab(\"orders\")}\r\n                  action\r\n                >\r\n                  My Orders\r\n                </ListGroup.Item>\r\n                <ListGroup.Item\r\n                  active={activeTab === \"edit\"}\r\n                  onClick={() => setActiveTab(\"edit\")}\r\n                  action\r\n                >\r\n                  Edit Profile\r\n                </ListGroup.Item>\r\n              </ListGroup>\r\n              <button className=\"btn btn-danger me-2 mt-3\" onClick={handleLogout}>\r\n                Logout\r\n              </button>\r\n            </Card.Body>\r\n          </Card>\r\n        </Col>\r\n\r\n        <Col md={9}>\r\n          <Card>\r\n            <Card.Body>\r\n              {activeTab === \"dashboard\" && (\r\n                <>\r\n                  <h4>Hello, {user?.fullname}</h4>\r\n                  <p>\r\n                    From your My Account Dashboard you have the ability to view a\r\n                    snapshot of your recent account activity and update your\r\n                    account information.\r\n                  </p>\r\n                  <Row>\r\n                    <Col md={4}>\r\n                      <Card className=\"p-3 text-center border-pink\">\r\n                        <h5>9882</h5>\r\n                        <p>Balance</p>\r\n                      </Card>\r\n                    </Col>\r\n                    <Col md={4}>\r\n                      <Card className=\"p-3 text-center border-pink\">\r\n                        <h5>118</h5>\r\n                        <p>Total Order Amount</p>\r\n                      </Card>\r\n                    </Col>\r\n                    <Col md={4}>\r\n                      <Card className=\"p-3 text-center border-pink\">\r\n                        <h5>{orders.length}</h5>\r\n                        <p>Total Orders</p>\r\n                      </Card>\r\n                    </Col>\r\n                  </Row>\r\n                </>\r\n              )}\r\n\r\n              {activeTab === \"orders\" && (\r\n                <div className=\"mt-4\">\r\n                  <h5>My Orders</h5>\r\n                  {loadingOrders ? (\r\n                    <div className=\"text-center py-4\">\r\n                      <Spinner animation=\"border\" />\r\n                    </div>\r\n                  ) : (\r\n                    <Table striped bordered hover>\r\n                      <thead>\r\n                        <tr>\r\n                          <th>#</th>\r\n                          <th>Order ID</th>\r\n                          <th>Date</th>\r\n                          <th>Status</th>\r\n                          <th>Total</th>\r\n                        </tr>\r\n                      </thead>\r\n                      <tbody>\r\n                        {orders.map((order, index) => (\r\n                          <tr key={order.id}>\r\n                            <td>{index + 1}</td>\r\n                            <td>#{order.id}</td>\r\n                            <td>{order.created_at?.split(\"T\")[0]}</td>\r\n                            <td>{order.status}</td>\r\n                            <td>{order.total} EGP</td>\r\n                          </tr>\r\n                        ))}\r\n                      </tbody>\r\n                    </Table>\r\n                  )}\r\n                </div>\r\n              )}\r\n\r\n              {activeTab === \"edit\" && (\r\n                <div className=\"mt-4\">\r\n                  <h5>Edit Profile</h5>\r\n                  <Form>\r\n                    <Form.Group controlId=\"fullName\">\r\n                      <Form.Label>Full Name</Form.Label>\r\n                      <Form.Control type=\"text\" defaultValue={user?.fullname || \"\"} />\r\n                    </Form.Group>\r\n                    <Form.Group controlId=\"email\" className=\"mt-3\">\r\n                      <Form.Label>Email</Form.Label>\r\n                      <Form.Control type=\"email\" defaultValue={user?.email || \"\"} />\r\n                    </Form.Group>\r\n                    <Form.Group controlId=\"phone\" className=\"mt-3\">\r\n                      <Form.Label>Phone</Form.Label>\r\n                      <Form.Control type=\"text\" defaultValue={user?.phone || \"\"} />\r\n                    </Form.Group>\r\n                    <Form.Group controlId=\"address\" className=\"mt-3\">\r\n                      <Form.Label>Address</Form.Label>\r\n                      <Form.Control type=\"text\" defaultValue=\"\" placeholder=\"Add your address...\" />\r\n                    </Form.Group>\r\n                    <Button className=\"mt-3 view\">Save Changes</Button>\r\n                  </Form>\r\n                </div>\r\n              )}\r\n            </Card.Body>\r\n          </Card>\r\n        </Col>\r\n      </Row>\r\n    </Container>\r\n  );\r\n};\r\n\r\nexport default Profile;\r\nhttps://yousab-tech.com/Florifliwer/public/api/auth/profile/update\r\nit is a post request wan to allow user update his profile \r\n*******************************************************************************************************************************************************************\r\nimport React from \"react\";\r\nimport \"bootstrap/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css\";\r\n\r\nconst Contact = () => {\r\n  return (\r\n    <div className=\"container my-5\">\r\n      <h2 className=\"fw-bold text-center mb-4\">Contact Us</h2>\r\n      <div className=\"row\">\r\n        {/* Google Maps Embed */}\r\n        <div className=\"col-md-6\">\r\n        <iframe\r\n            title=\"Fiori Flower Location\"\r\n            src=\"https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d879266.5438815374!2d30.03943537542964!3d30.587849416113393!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x145851e02b20d283%3A0xb3fecab4c53ab0ce!2z2YHZitmI2LHZiiDZgdmE2KfZiNix!5e0!3m2!1sen!2seg!4v1741726335912!5m2!1sen!2seg\"\r\n            width=\"100%\"\r\n            height=\"500\"\r\n            style={{ border: 0, borderRadius:\"10px\" }}\r\n            allowFullScreen=\"\"\r\n            loading=\"lazy\"\r\n            referrerPolicy=\"no-referrer-when-downgrade\"\r\n          ></iframe>\r\n\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        {/* Contact Form */}\r\n        <div className=\"col-md-6\">\r\n          <form className=\"p-4 border rounded shadow-sm bg-light\">\r\n            <div className=\"mb-3\">\r\n              <label className=\"form-label\">Name</label>\r\n              <input type=\"text\" className=\"form-control\" placeholder=\"Your Name\" required />\r\n            </div>\r\n\r\n            <div className=\"mb-3\">\r\n              <label className=\"form-label\">Email</label>\r\n              <input type=\"email\" className=\"form-control\" placeholder=\"Your Email\" required />\r\n            </div>\r\n\r\n            <div className=\"mb-3\">\r\n              <label className=\"form-label\">Phone</label>\r\n              <input type=\"tel\" className=\"form-control\" placeholder=\"Your Phone Number\" required />\r\n            </div>\r\n\r\n            <div className=\"mb-3\">\r\n              <label className=\"form-label\">Message</label>\r\n              <textarea className=\"form-control\" rows=\"4\" placeholder=\"Your Message\" required></textarea>\r\n            </div>\r\n\r\n            <button type=\"submit\" className=\"btn view w-100\">Send Message</button>\r\n          </form>\r\n        </div>\r\n      </div>\r\n    </div>\r\n  );\r\n};\r\n\r\nexport default Contact;\r\n\r\nhttps://yousab-tech.com/Florifliwer/public/api/message\r\nit is a post request wan to allow user send contact form \r\n***********************************************************************************************************************************************************\r\nimport React from \'react\';\r\nimport { FaFacebookF, FaInstagram } from \'react-icons/fa\';\r\nimport { LuSendHorizontal } from \"react-icons/lu\";\r\n\r\nconst Footer = () => {\r\n  return (\r\n    <footer id=\"colophon\" className=\"footer-container footer-area\">\r\n     \r\n        {/* Newsletter Section */}\r\n        <section className=\"elementor-section elementor-top-section\">\r\n          <div className=\"elementor-container\">\r\n            <div className=\"row align-items-center\">\r\n              {/* Newsletter Form */}\r\n              <div className=\"col-md-6\">\r\n                <div className=\"ts-mailchimp-subscription-shortcode text-light\">\r\n                  <section className=\"widget-container mailchimp-subscription\">\r\n                    <div className=\"widget-title-wrapper\">\r\n                      <h3 className=\"widget-title heading-title\">\r\n                        Join our newsletter and get…\r\n                      </h3>\r\n                      <div className=\"newsletter\">\r\n                        <p>\r\n                          Join our email subscription now to get updates on\r\n                          promotions and coupons.\r\n                        </p>\r\n                      </div>\r\n                    </div>\r\n                    <div className=\"subscribe-widget\">\r\n                    <form id=\"mc4wp-form-1\" className=\"mc4wp-form\" method=\"post\">\r\n                        <div className=\"mc4wp-form-fields\">\r\n                          <div className=\"input-group\">\r\n                            <input\r\n                              type=\"email\"\r\n                              name=\"EMAIL\"\r\n                              placeholder=\"Your email here...\"\r\n                              required\r\n                              className=\"form-control\"\r\n                            //   style={{ borderColor: pinkColor }}\r\n                            />\r\n                            <button\r\n                              className=\"send\"\r\n                              type=\"submit\"\r\n                            //   style={{ backgroundColor: pinkColor, color: \'#fff\' }}\r\n                            >\r\n                              <LuSendHorizontal />\r\n                            </button>\r\n                          </div>\r\n                        </div>\r\n                      </form>\r\n                    </div>\r\n                  </section>\r\n                </div>\r\n              </div>\r\n\r\n              {/* Social Icons */}\r\n              <div className=\"col-md-6 text-md-end mt-2\">\r\n                <div className=\"elementor-social-icons-wrapper\">\r\n                  <a\r\n                    className=\"elementor-icon elementor-social-icon\"\r\n                    href=\"https://www.facebook.com/FlowerPowerEG/\"\r\n                    target=\"_blank\"\r\n                    rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\r\n                  >\r\n                    <FaFacebookF />\r\n                  </a>\r\n                  <a\r\n                    className=\"elementor-icon elementor-social-icon\"\r\n                    href=\"https://www.instagram.com/flowerpowerdesign/\"\r\n                    target=\"_blank\"\r\n                    rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\r\n                  >\r\n                    <FaInstagram />\r\n                  </a>\r\n                </div>\r\n              </div>\r\n            </div>\r\n          </div>\r\n        </section>\r\n\r\n        {/* Divider */}\r\n        <div className=\"container\">\r\n        <section className=\"elementor-section\">\r\n          <div className=\"elementor-container\">\r\n            <div className=\"elementor-divider\">\r\n              <span className=\"elementor-divider-separator\"></span>\r\n            </div>\r\n          </div>\r\n        </section>\r\n\r\n        {/* Logo, Contact, and Payment Section */}\r\n        <section className=\"elementor-section\">\r\n          <div className=\"elementor-container\">\r\n            <div className=\"row\" style={{alignItems:\"center\"}}>\r\n              {/* Logo */}\r\n              <div className=\"col-md-4 text-center\">\r\n                <img\r\n                  src=\"/images/logo.jpg\"\r\n                  alt=\"Flower Power Logo\"\r\n                  className=\"img-fluid\"\r\n                  width=\"200\"\r\n                />\r\n              </div>\r\n\r\n              {/* Contact Info */}\r\n              <div className=\"col-md-4 text-center\">\r\n                <h6>Need help? Call us: (+2) 01277705777</h6>\r\n                <div className=\"elementor-spacer\"></div>\r\n                <p>Opening Hours: Daily, from 10am to 10pm</p>\r\n              </div>\r\n\r\n              {/* Payment Methods */}\r\n              <div className=\"col-md-4 text-center\">\r\n                <img\r\n                  src=\"https://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcRXk-YNzJCvteaQAPlXQxj2pHOFg_rgEmwSRuP6bCGlC9YkvfyxQVvNX-mOMWEmbwT_Q9w&usqp=CAU\"\r\n                  alt=\"Payment Methods\"\r\n                  className=\"img-fluid\"\r\n                  width=\"200\"\r\n                />\r\n              </div>\r\n            </div>\r\n          </div>\r\n        </section>\r\n\r\n        {/* Divider */}\r\n        <section className=\"elementor-section\">\r\n          <div className=\"elementor-container\">\r\n            <div className=\"elementor-divider\">\r\n              <span className=\"elementor-divider-separator\"></span>\r\n            </div>\r\n          </div>\r\n        </section>\r\n\r\n        {/* Copyright and Links Section */}\r\n        <section className=\"elementor-section\">\r\n          <div className=\"elementor-container\">\r\n            <div className=\"row\">\r\n              {/* Copyright */}\r\n              <div className=\"col-md-6 text-center text-md-start\">\r\n                <p>\r\n                  © <span style={{ color: \'#eb085b\' }}>Fiori Flower</span> – All\r\n                  Rights Reserved.\r\n                </p>\r\n              </div>\r\n\r\n              {/* Footer Links */}\r\n              <div className=\"col-md-6 text-center text-md-end\">\r\n                <ul className=\"list-inline\">\r\n                  <li className=\"list-inline-item\">\r\n                    <a href=\"/terms-and-conditions\">Terms and Conditions</a>\r\n                  </li>\r\n                  <li className=\"list-inline-item\">\r\n                    <a href=\"/privacy-policy\">Privacy Policy</a>\r\n                  </li>\r\n                  <li className=\"list-inline-item\">\r\n                    <a href=\"/contact-us\">Contact Us</a>\r\n                  </li>\r\n                  <li className=\"list-inline-item\">\r\n                    <a href=\"/about-us\">About Us</a>\r\n                  </li>\r\n                </ul>\r\n              </div>\r\n            </div>\r\n          </div>\r\n        </section>\r\n      </div>\r\n    </footer>\r\n  );\r\n};\r\n\r\nexport default Footer;\r\n\r\nhttps://yousab-tech.com/Florifliwer/public/api/newsletter\r\nit is a post request wan to allow user send newsletter form \r\n****************************************************************************************************************************************************\r\nimport React, { useState, useEffect } from \"react\";\r\nimport { NavLink, useLocation } from \"react-router-dom\";\r\nimport { GoPerson } from \"react-icons/go\";\r\nimport { MdOutlineShoppingCart } from \"react-icons/md\";\r\nimport { IoMenu } from \"react-icons/io5\";\r\nimport Button from \"react-bootstrap/Button\";\r\nimport Offcanvas from \"react-bootstrap/Offcanvas\";\r\nimport \"bootstrap/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css\";\r\nimport \"bootstrap/dist/js/bootstrap.bundle.min\";\r\nimport { useNavigate } from \"react-router-dom\";\r\n\r\nconst Header = () => {\r\n  const location = useLocation();\r\n  const [isLoginVisible, setIsLoginVisible] = useState(false);\r\n  const [cartTotal, setCartTotal] = useState(0);\r\n  const [showCart, setShowCart] = useState(false);\r\n  const [cartItems, setCartItems] = useState([]);\r\n  const [isLoggedIn, setIsLoggedIn] = useState(!!localStorage.getItem(\"token\"));\r\n  const [loginData, setLoginData] = useState({ email: \"\", password: \"\" });\r\n  const [userData, setUserData] = useState(null); // To hold user profile data\r\n  const navigate = useNavigate();// Hook for navigation\r\n  useEffect(() => {\r\n    setIsLoggedIn(!!localStorage.getItem(\"token\"));\r\n    if (isLoggedIn) {\r\n      fetchCartItems();\r\n      fetchUserData(); // Fetch user profile data after login\r\n    }\r\n  }, [isLoggedIn]);\r\n\r\n  const fetchCartItems = async () => {\r\n    const token = localStorage.getItem(\"token\");\r\n    if (!token) return;\r\n\r\n    try {\r\n      const response = await fetch(\"https://yousab-tech.com/Florifliwer/public/api/auth/cart\", {\r\n        method: \"GET\",\r\n        headers: {\r\n          \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\",\r\n          Authorization: `Bearer ${token}`\r\n        },\r\n      });\r\n\r\n      const data = await response.json();\r\n      if (data.cart) {\r\n        setCartItems(data.cart);\r\n        setCartTotal(data.total);\r\n      }\r\n    } catch (error) {\r\n      console.error(\"Error fetching cart items:\", error);\r\n    }\r\n  };\r\n\r\n  const fetchUserData = async () => {\r\n    const token = localStorage.getItem(\"token\");\r\n    if (!token) return;\r\n\r\n    try {\r\n      const response = await fetch(\"https://yousab-tech.com/Florifliwer/public/api/auth/user-profile\", {\r\n        method: \"GET\",\r\n        headers: {\r\n          \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\",\r\n          Authorization: `Bearer ${token}`\r\n        },\r\n      });\r\n\r\n      const data = await response.json();\r\n      if (data) {\r\n        setUserData(data);\r\n      }\r\n    } catch (error) {\r\n      console.error(\"Error fetching user data:\", error);\r\n    }\r\n  };\r\n\r\n  const handleLoginClick = () => {\r\n    setIsLoginVisible(!isLoginVisible);\r\n  };\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n  const handleChange = (e) => {\r\n    setLoginData({ ...loginData, [e.target.name]: e.target.value });\r\n  };\r\n\r\n  const handleLoginSubmit = async (e) => {\r\n    e.preventDefault();\r\n    try {\r\n      const response = await fetch(\"https://yousab-tech.com/Florifliwer/public/api/auth/login\", {\r\n        method: \"POST\",\r\n        headers: { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" },\r\n        body: JSON.stringify(loginData),\r\n      });\r\n      const data = await response.json();\r\n      if (data.token) {\r\n        localStorage.setItem(\"token\", data.token);\r\n        setIsLoggedIn(true);\r\n        setIsLoginVisible(false);\r\n        fetchCartItems(); // Fetch cart after login\r\n        fetchUserData(); // Fetch user profile data\r\n      } else {\r\n        alert(\"Invalid credentials\");\r\n      }\r\n    } catch (error) {\r\n      alert(error);\r\n    }\r\n  };\r\n\r\n\r\n  const handleRemoveFromCart = async (hash) => {\r\n    const token = localStorage.getItem(\"token\");\r\n    if (!token) return;\r\n  \r\n    try {\r\n      const response = await fetch(\"https://yousab-tech.com/Florifliwer/public/api/auth/remove/cart\", {\r\n        method: \"POST\",\r\n        headers: {\r\n          \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\",\r\n          Authorization: `Bearer ${token}`\r\n        },\r\n        body: JSON.stringify({ hash })\r\n      });\r\n  \r\n      const data = await response.json();\r\n      \r\n      if (data.success) {\r\n        // Update state by removing the deleted item\r\n        setCartItems(prevCartItems => prevCartItems.filter(item => item.hash !== hash));\r\n        setCartTotal(data.total); // Update total price\r\n      }\r\n    } catch (error) {\r\n      console.error(\"Error removing item from cart:\", error);\r\n    }\r\n  };\r\n\r\n  const handleUpdateQuantity = async (hash, action) => {\r\n    const token = localStorage.getItem(\"token\");\r\n    if (!token) return;\r\n  \r\n    const apiUrl = `https://yousab-tech.com/Florifliwer/public/api/auth/update/item/count?action=${action}`;\r\n  \r\n    try {\r\n      const response = await fetch(apiUrl, {\r\n        method: \"POST\",\r\n        headers: {\r\n          \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\",\r\n          Authorization: `Bearer ${token}`\r\n        },\r\n        body: JSON.stringify({ hash })\r\n      });\r\n  \r\n      const data = await response.json();\r\n  \r\n      if (data.success) {\r\n        // Update cart state\r\n        setCartItems(prevCartItems =>\r\n          prevCartItems.map(item =>\r\n            item.hash === hash ? { ...item, quantity: action === \"increment\" ? item.quantity + 1 : item.quantity - 1 } : item\r\n          )\r\n        );\r\n        setCartTotal(data.total);\r\n      }\r\n    } catch (error) {\r\n      console.error(`Error updating quantity: ${error}`);\r\n    }\r\n  };\r\n  \r\n  const handleIncrement = (hash) => {\r\n    handleUpdateQuantity(hash, \"increment\");\r\n  };\r\n  \r\n  const handleDecrement = (hash) => {\r\n    handleUpdateQuantity(hash, \"decrement\");\r\n  };\r\n\r\n  const handleProfileClick = () => {\r\n    navigate(\"/profile\");// Navigate to the profile page\r\n  };\r\n  \r\n\r\n  return (\r\n    <header className=\"ts-header sticky-top bg-white shadow-sm\">\r\n      <div className=\"container d-flex align-items-center justify-content-between py-2\">\r\n        <button className=\"btn d-lg-none\" data-bs-toggle=\"offcanvas\" data-bs-target=\"#mobileMenu\">\r\n          <IoMenu color=\"#eb085b\" />\r\n        </button>\r\n\r\n        <NavLink to=\"/\" className=\"navbar-brand\">\r\n          <img src=\"/images/logo.png\" height={\"100px\"} alt=\"Flower Power\" />\r\n        </NavLink>\r\n\r\n        {/* Desktop Navigation */}\r\n        <nav className=\"d-none d-lg-block\">\r\n          <ul className=\"nav\">\r\n            <li className=\"nav-item\">\r\n              <NavLink className=\"nav-link\" to=\"/\" activeClassName=\"active-link\">\r\n                Home\r\n              </NavLink>\r\n            </li>\r\n            <li className=\"nav-item dropdown\">\r\n              <a\r\n                className=\"nav-link dropdown-toggle\"\r\n                href=\"#\"\r\n                id=\"shopDropdown\"\r\n                role=\"button\"\r\n                data-bs-toggle=\"dropdown\"\r\n                aria-expanded=\"false\"\r\n              >\r\n                Shop\r\n              </a>\r\n              <ul className=\"dropdown-menu\" aria-labelledby=\"shopDropdown\">\r\n                <li>\r\n                  <NavLink className=\"dropdown-item\" to=\"/product-category/complete-collection\" activeClassName=\"active-link\">\r\n                    Complete Collection\r\n                  </NavLink>\r\n                </li>\r\n                <li>\r\n                  <NavLink className=\"dropdown-item\" to=\"/product-category/arrangements\" activeClassName=\"active-link\">\r\n                    Arrangements\r\n                  </NavLink>\r\n                </li>\r\n                <li>\r\n                  <NavLink className=\"dropdown-item\" to=\"/product-category/bouquets\" activeClassName=\"active-link\">\r\n                    Bouquets\r\n                  </NavLink>\r\n                </li>\r\n                <li>\r\n                  <NavLink className=\"dropdown-item\" to=\"/product-category/boxes\" activeClassName=\"active-link\">\r\n                    Boxes\r\n                  </NavLink>\r\n                </li>\r\n              </ul>\r\n            </li>\r\n            <li className=\"nav-item\">\r\n              <NavLink className=\"nav-link\" to=\"/about\" activeClassName=\"active-link\">\r\n                About Us\r\n              </NavLink>\r\n            </li>\r\n            <li className=\"nav-item\">\r\n              <NavLink className=\"nav-link\" to=\"/about-us\" activeClassName=\"active-link\">\r\n               Occasions\r\n              </NavLink>\r\n            </li>\r\n            <li className=\"nav-item dropdown\">\r\n              <a\r\n                className=\"nav-link dropdown-toggle\"\r\n                href=\"#\"\r\n                id=\"shopDropdown\"\r\n                role=\"button\"\r\n                data-bs-toggle=\"dropdown\"\r\n                aria-expanded=\"false\"\r\n              >\r\n                Our Services\r\n              </a>\r\n              <ul className=\"dropdown-menu\" aria-labelledby=\"shopDropdown\">\r\n                <li>\r\n                  <NavLink className=\"dropdown-item\" to=\"/product-category/complete-collection\" activeClassName=\"active-link\">\r\n                    Complete Collection\r\n                  </NavLink>\r\n                </li>\r\n                <li>\r\n                  <NavLink className=\"dropdown-item\" to=\"/product-category/arrangements\" activeClassName=\"active-link\">\r\n                    Arrangements\r\n                  </NavLink>\r\n                </li>\r\n                <li>\r\n                  <NavLink className=\"dropdown-item\" to=\"/product-category/bouquets\" activeClassName=\"active-link\">\r\n                    Bouquets\r\n                  </NavLink>\r\n                </li>\r\n                <li>\r\n                  <NavLink className=\"dropdown-item\" to=\"/product-category/boxes\" activeClassName=\"active-link\">\r\n                    Boxes\r\n                  </NavLink>\r\n                </li>\r\n              </ul>\r\n            </li>\r\n            <li className=\"nav-item\">\r\n              <NavLink className=\"nav-link\" to=\"/contact\" activeClassName=\"active-link\">\r\n                Contact Us\r\n              </NavLink>\r\n            </li>\r\n          </ul>\r\n        </nav>\r\n\r\n        <div className=\"d-flex align-items-center\">\r\n          <div className=\"position-relative\">\r\n          <div className=\"d-flex align-items-center\">\r\n            {/* If not logged in, show login button */}\r\n            {!isLoggedIn ? (\r\n              <button className=\"btn btn-outline-secondary me-2\" onClick={handleLoginClick}>\r\n                <GoPerson style={{ color: \"#eb085b\" }} />\r\n              </button>\r\n            ) : (\r\n              <div className=\"profile-area\" onClick={handleProfileClick} style={{ cursor: \'pointer\' }}>\r\n                {/* Displaying user profile image */}\r\n                <img \r\n                  src={userData?.image || \"/images/default-profile.png\"} \r\n                  alt=\"Profile\"\r\n                  className=\"rounded-circle mx-4\"\r\n                  style={{ width: \"60px\", height: \"60px\", objectFit: \"cover\" }}\r\n                />\r\n              </div>\r\n            )}\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n\r\n            {isLoginVisible && (\r\n              <div className=\"account-dropdown-form dropdown-container position-absolute top-100 end-0 mt-2\">\r\n                <div className=\"form-content bg-white p-4 shadow border rounded\">\r\n                  <h2 className=\"dropdown-title mb-3\">Login</h2>\r\n                  <form onSubmit={handleLoginSubmit}>\r\n                    <p>\r\n                      <label>Email</label>\r\n                      <input\r\n                        type=\"email\"\r\n                        name=\"email\"\r\n                        value={loginData.email}\r\n                        onChange={handleChange}\r\n                        className=\"form-control\"\r\n                      />\r\n                    </p>\r\n                    <p>\r\n                      <label>Password</label>\r\n                      <input\r\n                        type=\"password\"\r\n                        name=\"password\"\r\n                        value={loginData.password}\r\n                        onChange={handleChange}\r\n                        className=\"form-control\"\r\n                      />\r\n                    </p>\r\n                    <button type=\"submit\" className=\"btn addtocart w-100\">\r\n                      Log In\r\n                    </button>\r\n                  </form>\r\n                  <div className=\"text-center mt-2\">\r\n                    <NavLink to=\"/register\">Create an account</NavLink>\r\n                  </div>\r\n                </div>\r\n              </div>\r\n            )}\r\n          </div>\r\n\r\n          <button className=\"btn btn-outline-secondary me-2\" onClick={() => setShowCart(true)}>\r\n            <MdOutlineShoppingCart />\r\n            {cartItems.length > 0 && (\r\n              <span className=\"badge bg-danger rounded-pill ms-1\">{cartItems.length}</span>\r\n            )}\r\n          </button>\r\n        </div>\r\n      </div>\r\n\r\n      <Offcanvas show={showCart} onHide={() => setShowCart(false)} placement=\"end\">\r\n        <Offcanvas.Header closeButton>\r\n          <Offcanvas.Title>Cart</Offcanvas.Title>\r\n        </Offcanvas.Header>\r\n        <Offcanvas.Body>\r\n\r\n                    {/* Cart Items */}\r\n                    <div className=\"cart-wrapper\">\r\n            <div className=\"cart-content\">\r\n              <ul className=\"cart_list\">\r\n              {cartItems.length > 0 ? (\r\n            <ul className=\"list-group\">\r\n              {cartItems.map((item) => (\r\n              <li key={item.hash} className=\"woocommerce-mini-cart-item mb-3\">\r\n              <a className=\"thumbnail\" href={`/product/${item.id}`}>\r\n                <img\r\n                  src={item.image}\r\n                  alt={item.title}\r\n                  className=\"img-fluid rounded\"\r\n                  style={{ width: \"80px\", height: \"80px\", objectFit: \"cover\" }}\r\n                />\r\n              </a>\r\n              <div className=\"cart-item-wrapper ms-3\">\r\n                <h3 className=\"product-name h6 mb-1\">\r\n                  <a href={`/product/${item.id}`}>{item.title}</a>\r\n                </h3>\r\n                <span className=\"price text-muted\">\r\n                  <bdi>{item.price.toFixed(2)}&nbsp;EGP</bdi>\r\n                </span>\r\n                <div className=\"quantity mt-2\">\r\n                  <div className=\"number-button d-flex align-items-center text-center px-5\">\r\n                    <button\r\n                      className=\"btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary minus\"\r\n                      onClick={() => handleDecrement(item.hash)}\r\n                      disabled={item.quantity <= 1} // Prevent negative values\r\n                    >\r\n                      -\r\n                    </button>\r\n                    <input\r\n                      type=\"number\"\r\n                      className=\"form-control form-control-sm mx-2 text-center\"\r\n                      value={item.quantity}\r\n                      readOnly\r\n                      style={{ width: \"60px\" }}\r\n                    />\r\n                    <button\r\n                      className=\"btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary plus\"\r\n                      onClick={() => handleIncrement(item.hash)}\r\n                    >\r\n                      +\r\n                    </button>\r\n                  </div>\r\n                </div>\r\n\r\n                <div className=\"subtotal mt-2\">\r\n                  <bdi>{(item.price * item.quantity).toFixed(2)}&nbsp;EGP</bdi>\r\n                </div>\r\n                <button className=\"btn mt-2 remove_from_cart_button view\" onClick={() => handleRemoveFromCart(item.hash)}>\r\n                  × Remove\r\n                </button>\r\n              </div>\r\n              </li>\r\n              ))}\r\n            </ul>\r\n\r\n            \r\n          ) : (\r\n            <p>Your cart is empty</p>\r\n          )}\r\n              </ul>\r\n\r\n              {/* Cart Footer */}\r\n              <div className=\"dropdown-footer mt-4\">\r\n                <div className=\"total d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center mb-3\">\r\n                  <span className=\"total-title\">Subtotal:</span>\r\n                  <span className=\"woocommerce-Price-amount amount fw-bold\">\r\n                    <bdi>{cartTotal.toFixed(2)}&nbsp;EGP</bdi>\r\n                  </span>\r\n                </div>\r\n                <div className=\"d-grid gap-2\">\r\n                  {/* <a href=\"/cart\" className=\"btn btn-outline-secondary\">\r\n                    View Cart\r\n                  </a> */}\r\n                  <a href=\"/checkout\" className=\"btn view\">\r\n                    Checkout\r\n                  </a>\r\n                </div>\r\n              </div>\r\n            </div>\r\n          </div>\r\n\r\n        </Offcanvas.Body>\r\n      </Offcanvas>\r\n\r\n\r\n            {/* Offcanvas Mobile Menu */}\r\n            <div className=\"offcanvas offcanvas-start\" id=\"mobileMenu\" tabIndex=\"-1\">\r\n        <div className=\"offcanvas-header\">\r\n          <h5 className=\"offcanvas-title\">Menu</h5>\r\n          <button type=\"button\" className=\"btn-close\" data-bs-dismiss=\"offcanvas\"></button>\r\n        </div>\r\n        <div className=\"offcanvas-body\">\r\n          <ul className=\"nav flex-column\">\r\n            <li className=\"nav-item\">\r\n              <NavLink className=\"nav-link\" to=\"/\" activeClassName=\"active-link\">\r\n                Home\r\n              </NavLink>\r\n            </li>\r\n\r\n            {/* Mobile Shop Dropdown */}\r\n            <li className=\"nav-item\">\r\n              <a\r\n                className=\"nav-link dropdown-toggle\"\r\n                href=\"#mobileShopDropdown\"\r\n                data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\"\r\n                role=\"button\"\r\n                aria-expanded=\"false\"\r\n                aria-controls=\"mobileShopDropdown\"\r\n              >\r\n                Shop\r\n              </a>\r\n              <div className=\"collapse\" id=\"mobileShopDropdown\">\r\n                <ul className=\"nav flex-column ps-3\">\r\n                  <li>\r\n                    <NavLink className=\"nav-link\" to=\"/product-category/complete-collection\" activeClassName=\"active-link\">\r\n                      Complete Collection\r\n                    </NavLink>\r\n                  </li>\r\n                  <li>\r\n                    <NavLink className=\"nav-link\" to=\"/product-category/arrangements\" activeClassName=\"active-link\">\r\n                      Arrangements\r\n                    </NavLink>\r\n                  </li>\r\n                  <li>\r\n                    <NavLink className=\"nav-link\" to=\"/product-category/bouquets\" activeClassName=\"active-link\">\r\n                      Bouquets\r\n                    </NavLink>\r\n                  </li>\r\n                  <li>\r\n                    <NavLink className=\"nav-link\" to=\"/product-category/boxes\" activeClassName=\"active-link\">\r\n                      Boxes\r\n                    </NavLink>\r\n                  </li>\r\n                </ul>\r\n              </div>\r\n            </li>\r\n\r\n            <li className=\"nav-item\">\r\n              <NavLink className=\"nav-link\" to=\"/about-us\" activeClassName=\"active-link\">\r\n                About Us\r\n              </NavLink>\r\n            </li>\r\n            <li className=\"nav-item\">\r\n              <NavLink className=\"nav-link\" to=\"/contact-us\" activeClassName=\"active-link\">\r\n                Contact Us\r\n              </NavLink>\r\n            </li>\r\n          </ul>\r\n        </div>\r\n      </div>\r\n\r\n      {/* Active Link Styling */}\r\n      <style>\r\n        {`\r\n          .nav-link.active-link {\r\n            color: black !important;\r\n            font-weight: bold;\r\n          }\r\n\r\n          .dropdown-item.active-link {\r\n            color: black !important;\r\n            font-weight: bold;\r\n          }\r\n        `}\r\n      </style>\r\n    </header>\r\n  );\r\n};\r\n\r\nexport default Header;\r\nwant to categories inside shop\r\nhttps://yousab-tech.com/Florifliwer/public/api/categories	\r\n{\r\n\"status\": 200,\r\n\"message\": \"success\",\r\n\"data\": {\r\n\"categories\": [\r\n{\r\n\"id\": 1,\r\n\"title\": \"زهور طبيعية\",\r\n\"image\": \"https://yousab-tech.com/Florifliwer/public/default.jpg\"\r\n},\r\n{\r\n\"id\": 2,\r\n\"title\": \"زهور صناعية\",\r\n\"image\": \"https://yousab-tech.com/Florifliwer/public/default.jpg\"\r\n},\r\n{\r\n\"id\": 3,\r\n\"title\": \"باقات زهور\",\r\n\"image\": \"https://yousab-tech.com/Florifliwer/public/default.jpg\"\r\n},\r\n{\r\n\"id\": 4,\r\n\"title\": \"زهور الزفاف\",\r\n\"image\": \"https://yousab-tech.com/Florifliwer/public/default.jpg\"\r\n},\r\n{\r\n\"id\": 5,\r\n\"title\": \"زهور أعياد الميلاد\",\r\n\"image\": \"https://yousab-tech.com/Florifliwer/public/default.jpg\"\r\n},\r\n{\r\n\"id\": 6,\r\n\"title\": \"زهور المناسبات\",\r\n\"image\": \"https://yousab-tech.com/Florifliwer/public/default.jpg\"\r\n},\r\n{\r\n\"id\": 7,\r\n\"title\": \"زهور عيد الحب\",\r\n\"image\": \"https://yousab-tech.com/Florifliwer/public/default.jpg\"\r\n},\r\n{\r\n\"id\": 8,\r\n\"title\": \"نباتات داخلية\",\r\n\"image\": \"https://yousab-tech.com/Florifliwer/public/default.jpg\"\r\n},\r\n{\r\n\"id\": 9,\r\n\"title\": \"نباتات خارجية\",\r\n\"image\": \"https://yousab-tech.com/Florifliwer/public/default.jpg\"\r\n},\r\n{\r\n\"id\": 10,\r\n\"title\": \"إكسسوارات زهور\",\r\n\"image\": \"https://yousab-tech.com/Florifliwer/public/default.jpg\"\r\n}\r\n]\r\n}\r\n}\r\n*************************************************************************************************************\r\nto show subcategories of a category https://yousab-tech.com/Florifliwer/public/api/categorySubcategories?category_id=2&per_page=5\r\n{\r\n\"pagination\": {\r\n\"current_page\": 1,\r\n\"per_page\": 5,\r\n\"last_page\": 1,\r\n\"total_items\": 3\r\n},\r\n\"data\": [\r\n{\r\n\"id\": 3,\r\n\"title\": \"توليب\",\r\n\"category\": {\r\n\"id\": 2,\r\n\"title\": \"زهور صناعية\",\r\n\"image\": \"https://yousab-tech.com/Florifliwer/public/default.jpg\"\r\n}\r\n},\r\n{\r\n\"id\": 8,\r\n\"title\": \"هيدرانجيا\",\r\n\"category\": {\r\n\"id\": 2,\r\n\"title\": \"زهور صناعية\",\r\n\"image\": \"https://yousab-tech.com/Florifliwer/public/default.jpg\"\r\n}\r\n},\r\n{\r\n\"id\": 9,\r\n\"title\": \"فاوانيا\",\r\n\"category\": {\r\n\"id\": 2,\r\n\"title\": \"زهور صناعية\",\r\n\"image\": \"https://yousab-tech.com/Florifliwer/public/default.jpg\"\r\n}\r\n}\r\n]\r\n}\r\n**************************************************************************************************************\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nV','2025-03-31 07:10:56','2025-08-16 03:36:34',1,0,1),(66,'Holly Mass','Fgfhj','فهرس القداس  بالطقوس \r\nرفع بخور عشية باكر(اللبس الاسود)\r\nصلاة الاستعداد \r\nصلاة بعد الاستعداد 2 (اختيار خبز الحمل)\r\nمجدا واكراما \r\nالليلويا فاي بيه بي \r\nرشومات الحمل 2 \r\nذوكصابتري \r\nصلاة الشكر4\r\nصلاة التقدمة (تقال سرا)\r\nتحليل الخدام(عبيدك خدام هذا اليوم) \r\nسر بخور البولس (يا الله العظيم الابدي)\r\nطاي شوري \r\nالهيتنيهات \r\nتين اووأوشت\r\nالبولس \r\nالكاثوليكون \r\nبي اهموت غار  \r\nالابركسيس\r\nالسنكسار\r\nقدوس الله\r\nسر الانجيل 3\r\nصلاة الحجاب (عن حياة العالم)\r\nأوشية الانجيل 2\r\nمرد الانجيل السنوي \r\n*******************************************\r\nالوعظة\r\nسارية جون\r\nإنصوفيا (قانون الايمان)\r\nصلاة الصلح 2 (جبل الانسان علي غير فساد)\r\nصلاة صلح اخري3 \r\nالاسبزمس الآدام (افرحي يا مريم)\r\nقبلوا بعضكم بعضا \r\nبشفاعات \r\nمستحق وعادل 2\r\nالذي يقف امامه \r\nالاسبزمس الواطس(الشاروبيم يسجد لك) \r\nقدوس قدوس \r\nتجسد وتانس \r\nوقام من الاموات \r\nالرشومات 6\r\n الرشومات 2 (اخذ خبزا علي يديه الطاهرتين)\r\nامين امين امين بموتك يا رب نبشر\r\nسجود\r\nأوشية السلام (اذكر يا رب سلام كنيستك)\r\nأوشية الاباء (صلوا من اجل رئيس كهنتنا)\r\nأوشية القسوس(صلوا من اجل القمامصة)\r\nأوشية الموضع (خلاص هذا الموضع المقدس)\r\nصلاة المياه (مياه النهر هذه السنة باركها)\r\nأوشية الزروع (تفضل يا رب الزروع والعشب)\r\nأوشية اهوية السماء \r\nاصعدها كمقدارها \r\n(أوشية القربين (اذكر يا رب الذين قدموا لك\r\nأوشية حلول الروح القدس\r\n\r\n*******************************************\r\nالمجمع 4 (ابائنا القديسين ورؤساء الاباء)\r\nالترحيم 2 (أنبا بولا) (العطا)\r\nالقارئون فليقولون\r\nاذكر نفس عبدك نسيم سليمان يوسف\r\nاولئك يا رب \r\nكما كان \r\nسجود\r\nصلاة قبل ابانا الذي (الثلاث تقديسات)\r\nابانا الذي \r\nسجود\r\nصلاة بعد ابانا الذي (نعم نسالك ايها الاب)\r\nصلاة خضوع للاب(ننصت بخوف الله)\r\nصلاة تحليل للاب 2\r\nأوشية الاجتماعات (اذكر يا رب اجتماعتنا)\r\nمقدمة الاعتراف(جسد ودم حقيقي)\r\nالاعتراف 2\r\nالمزمور 150 2 (اطلبوا عنا وعن كل)\r\nبي أويك \r\nصلاة شكر بعد التناول \r\nصلاة وضع يد بعد التناول\r\nالتسريح 4\r\n*******************************************\r\nاللفافة بتبقا تحت للازازة واللي معاه الدم ع اليمين والمياه ع الشمال \n1-ابونا بيغسل ايده بعد قرايت الاجبية\r\n2-فيه لفة بعد الازازتين\nبتجيب الشرية لابونا وتقف جنبه علي يمينه \r\n3-تلات لفات بالانجيل الحديد والرابعة ترجع ترفعه من غير كلام وبتسجد في اخرهم وتقوم بسرعة وبعدها القراءات \r\n4-الشورية بعد الكاثوليك وبتلف تلات لفات بالإنجيل الحديد \r\n5-الشورية بعد السنكسار والانجيل الحديد وصلوا من اجل الانجيل المقدس وجملة قبل الانجيل قبطي استاسيتي رابيؤة انجليو\r\n\r\n6-وهوا الانجيل بيتقري بتمسك الشورية لابونا يحط بخور وبتديها لابونا تاني \r\n7-ابونا بيدي الشورية للشماش في نهاية الإنجيل\r\n8-ابونا بيغسل ايده بعد الوعظة\r\n9-بعد قبلوا بنلم الفوط ونحط عليه الصليب الحديد والإنجيل\r\n10-في الرشومات الشماس بيرفع صليب \r\nفيه شورية بعد كرحمتك يا رب \r\n11-بعد الجسد بنطبق الفافات \r\n12-بعد الدم بتستني ابونا لما يمسك الصنية عشان تمسح الاواني\r\n\r\nاوقات الشورية\r\nقبل القراءات\r\nبعد الكاثوليك\r\nبعد السنكسار\r\nعند واثناء قراءة الانجيل\r\nبعد كرحمتك يا رب \r\n\r\nالجسد بيتشال وبنوقف في النص في وش ابونا \r\nابقي احفظ مقدمة الانجيل\r\n\r\nايه الفرق بين المجمع والترحيم ؟','2025-03-31 07:11:15','2025-12-19 17:15:33',1,1,1),(67,'Marketting Refrence','','Marketting Reference\r\nGoogle Analytics\r\nUsed to know stats about your website visitors without having google ads\r\nGoogle business profile\r\n1-signup for business profile\r\n2-create a profile\r\n3- google business profile can be used instead of a website in google ads\r\n4- postal code should be accurate\r\n5- verify your account using sms code instead of videos\r\n6- you may need to apply for appeal to solve suspende google bussiness profile account and you will need to provide some document like ID or Passport, add evidence, wait for approved and unapproved\r\n7- to fix not publicly visible issue you have to fill all data even optional, click get verified, use phone code option instead of video, wait even for a month\r\nGoogle ads\r\nIt is vital to add keywords in meta keywords and description to search fro them even if there is no google ad created\r\nAdd headlines from keywords to make add stronger\r\nChange location options in campaign settings locations to  to presence: people in or regularly in your included locations\r\nWhen select locations use location option not radius to be more specific\r\n\r\nChange maximize clicks bid limit in campaign settings 5 EGP\r\nGoogle Add has main three types most important one is Sarch\r\nYou started with a wrong expensive one named performance max\r\nAll types\r\n\r\n1-Search Get in front of high-intent customers at the right time on Google Search\r\n1-Performance MaxReach audiences across all of Google with a single campaign.\r\n2-Demand Gen Drive demand and conversions on YouTube, Discover and Gmail with image and video ads\r\n3-Display Reach customers across 3 million sites and apps with engaging creative\r\n4-Shopping Showcase your products to shoppers as they explore what to buy\r\n5-Shopping Showcase your products to shoppers as they explore what to buy\r\n6-Video Reach viewers on YouTube and get conversions\r\n7-App Drive downloads and grow engagement for your app\r\n8-Smart Reach customers with a one-stop solution built for small businesses\r\nGoogle add opjectives\r\n1-SalesDrive sales online, in app, by phone, or in store\r\n2-LeadsGet leads and other conversions by encouraging customers to take action\r\n3-Website trafficGet the right people to visit your website\r\n4-App promotionGet more installs, engagement and pre-registration for your app\r\n5-Awareness and considerationReach a broad audience and build interest in your products or brand\r\n6-Local store visits and promotionsDrive visits to local stores, including restaurants and dealerships.\r\n7-Create a campaign without a goal\'s guidanceChoose a campaign type first, without a recommendation based on your objective.\r\nThere is an option that can be used to verify your identity to increase google trust but you will need some documents\r\nThere many ways to determine your targeted locations\r\n\r\nDiffrence between google add and SEO\r\n1- ad badge\r\n2-seo can uplevel on google add and also google add can uplevel on seo\r\n3-google ad avoid you optimizing website seo but cost a lot of money\r\n4-seo make you create less google ads\r\n5- clients types are two one search for you and other you search for him .google ad is the first type and facebook ad is the second\r\n6-google add clients are more likely to buy more than facebook clients\r\n7-google ads depends on keywords searchy\r\n8- google add types\r\nKeywoprd ad\r\nVideo youtube on specific videos\r\nAds as video in youtube\r\nBanner google ads (google adsense)\r\nNote: we can gain money from google adsense using my website\r\nThere is specific time to determine showing your add to avoid big costs \r\nThere is a revise option to revise all the add\r\nNote: you have to target specific audience in specific interval of time \r\nGoogle take money on cpc cost per click \r\nGoogle adsense\r\nTry to gain passive money out of it\r\nFacebook ads\r\nYou need to design well designed posts\r\nSearch engine optimization\r\nYou need to verifiy your authority for the website by adding some text to code or by adding something on server to dns\r\nYou can access dns in hostigator from domains>advanced tools>advanced dns manage\r\nGoogle marketing platforms\r\nSEO\r\nSEM\r\nGoogle Ad\r\nGoogle Analytics\r\nGoogle Business Profile\r\nGoogle Merchant Center\r\nCustomer persona\r\nIts described as collecting data about your customers and determine their foals and what are the boundaries that prevent them from achieving their goals\r\nMarketing stages\r\nAwareness\r\nConsideration\r\nConversion\r\nLoyalty\r\nAwareness\r\nSearch Engine Marketing\r\nSocial Media Marketing\r\nSocial Media Advertising\r\nInfluencer Marketing\r\nKey Takeaways\r\nConsideration\r\nUnique selling proposition\r\nTestimonials\r\nCase studies\r\nRemarketing ads\r\nWebinars\r\nEmail Marketing\r\nSocial media marketing\r\nFree trial\r\nConversion\r\nOptimize the checkout process\r\nAdd better photos\r\nStrengthen the copy\r\nAdd live chat\r\nPursue abandoned Carts\r\nIncrease website speed\r\nOffer a trial or money back guarantee\r\nExperiment with A/B test \r\nLoyalty\r\nSocial shares\r\nEncourage reviews\r\nSend freebies\r\nRemark customers with other products\r\nKey takeaways\r\n\r\nSocial Marketing Design Tools \r\nhttps://www.canva.com/ \r\nhttps://www.facebook.com/100086214113943/posts/pfbid0G1TRJ662RpTXrZxAdWUBRcUrFtL9gsfe5nc3T5i26m2FAMpXUddYFLYMmfV2muWZl/?mibextid=Nif5oz \r\nNotes\r\n1- show client that you cannot add call us option currently \r\n2- use chat gpt and you have to make your add get excellent score before publishing it \r\n3-  \r\nGoogle business profile general questions\r\n\r\nHere’s a comprehensive list of frequently asked questions (FAQs) and answers about Google Business Profile (GBP), covering everything from setup to advanced optimization techniques:\r\n\r\nGoogle Business Profile Basics\r\n1. What is Google Business Profile (GBP)?\r\nGoogle Business Profile (formerly known as Google My Business) is a free tool that helps businesses manage their online presence across Google, including Search and Maps. It allows businesses to display important information like business hours, location, contact details, and customer reviews.\r\n\r\n2. Why should I use Google Business Profile?\r\nUsing GBP improves your local SEO, helps potential customers find your business more easily, and provides an opportunity to manage customer reviews and engage with your audience. It also helps your business appear in Google Maps and the Local Pack on search results.\r\n\r\n3. How do I create a Google Business Profile?\r\nTo create a GBP:\r\n\r\nSign in to your Google account.\r\nGo to Google Business Profile.\r\nClick \"Manage now\" and follow the instructions to enter your business information.\r\nVerify your business through one of the available methods (postcard, phone, or email).\r\n4. What business types can use Google Business Profile?\r\nAlmost any type of business with a physical location or that serves customers face-to-face (including service-area businesses) can use GBP. This includes brick-and-mortar stores, restaurants, professional services (lawyers, plumbers, etc.), and more.\r\n\r\n5. How long does it take to verify my business on Google?\r\nDepending on the verification method you choose (postcard, phone, or email), verification can take anywhere from a few minutes to a few weeks. Most commonly, businesses verify via postcard, which typically arrives within 5-14 days.\r\n\r\nGoogle Business Profile Features\r\n6. What information can I display on my Google Business Profile?\r\nYou can display a variety of information, including:\r\n\r\nBusiness name, address, and phone number.\r\nHours of operation (including special hours).\r\nWebsite link.\r\nPhotos and videos.\r\nBusiness description.\r\nCategories and services/products.\r\nReviews and responses.\r\nQ&A section.\r\n7. Can I add multiple locations to my Google Business Profile?\r\nYes, if you have multiple business locations, you can manage all of them under a single Google account. Simply add each location by going to the \"Manage Locations\" tab in your GBP dashboard and clicking \"Add location.\"\r\n\r\n8. How do I update my business hours on Google Business Profile?\r\nTo update your hours:\r\n\r\nLog in to your GBP account.\r\nSelect the location you want to update.\r\nClick “Info” and find the section for \"Hours.\"\r\nEdit the hours and save changes.\r\n9. Can I post updates or promotions on my Google Business Profile?\r\nYes, Google Business Profile allows you to post updates, promotions, events, and news using the “Posts” feature. Posts show up on your business listing in Google Search and Maps, providing an additional way to engage with customers.\r\n\r\n10. What types of posts can I create on GBP?\r\nThe types of posts you can create include:\r\n\r\nWhat\'s new: Announcements or updates.\r\nEvent: Details about an upcoming event.\r\nOffer: Special promotions or discounts.\r\nProduct: Showcase a new or featured product.\r\nGoogle Business Profile and SEO\r\n11. How does Google Business Profile help with local SEO?\r\nA well-optimized GBP helps improve your business\'s visibility in local search results, especially in Google Maps and the Local Pack (the top 3 business listings that appear in a local search). Ensuring accurate and up-to-date information, getting positive reviews, and regularly posting updates can all improve your local SEO.\r\n\r\n12. What is the Local Pack in Google Search?\r\nThe Local Pack is the section in Google Search that shows the top three local businesses related to a user\'s search query, along with their Google Business Profiles. Appearing in the Local Pack can drive significant traffic to your business.\r\n\r\n13. How do I optimize my Google Business Profile for SEO?\r\nKey ways to optimize your GBP include:\r\n\r\nEnsuring all business information is complete and accurate.\r\nSelecting the most relevant business categories.\r\nAdding high-quality photos and videos.\r\nRegularly updating your profile with posts and offers.\r\nCollecting and responding to customer reviews.\r\nUsing keywords in your business description and posts.\r\nEnsuring your business name, address, and phone number (NAP) are consistent across the web.\r\n14. How important are reviews for Google Business Profile SEO?\r\nReviews are crucial for local SEO. Positive reviews signal to Google that your business is reputable and relevant, which can improve your ranking in search results. Engaging with both positive and negative reviews also shows that you value customer feedback.\r\n\r\n15. What is the impact of citations on local SEO and Google Business Profile?\r\nCitations are mentions of your business name, address, and phone number (NAP) across the web. Consistent citations on other websites (like Yelp, Facebook, and local directories) help reinforce your business’s legitimacy and improve your GBP rankings.\r\n\r\nGoogle Business Profile Photos and Videos\r\n16. How do I add photos to my Google Business Profile?\r\nTo add photos:\r\n\r\nSign in to your GBP account.\r\nGo to the location you\'d like to add photos to.\r\nClick \"Photos\" in the menu.\r\nUpload photos from your computer or mobile device.\r\n17. What types of photos should I upload to my Google Business Profile?\r\nLogo: For brand recognition.\r\nCover photo: The main image customers see in your business listing.\r\nInterior and exterior photos: Help customers recognize your business and understand what to expect.\r\nProduct or service photos: Showcase what your business offers.\r\nTeam photos: Add a personal touch by introducing your staff.\r\n18. Can I add videos to my Google Business Profile?\r\nYes, you can add videos up to 30 seconds long to your GBP. Videos are a great way to showcase your business, products, services, or customer testimonials.\r\n\r\n19. How do customer-uploaded photos impact my Google Business Profile?\r\nCustomers can upload their own photos when they visit your business, which will appear alongside your own photos. High-quality, positive photos from customers can enhance your profile’s appearance and attract more customers.\r\n\r\n20. What are photo and video guidelines for Google Business Profile?\r\nPhotos should be well-lit and represent your business accurately.\r\nImage resolution: Minimum 720x720 pixels.\r\nVideo length: Up to 30 seconds.\r\nVideo size: Maximum 100 MB.\r\nGoogle Business Profile Reviews\r\n21. How do I get customer reviews on my Google Business Profile?\r\nEncourage satisfied customers to leave reviews by:\r\n\r\nAsking for reviews in person or via email.\r\nSending customers a link to your GBP review section.\r\nDisplaying a \"Leave us a review\" sign at your location.\r\n22. How do I respond to reviews on my Google Business Profile?\r\nTo respond to reviews:\r\n\r\nSign in to your GBP account.\r\nClick “Reviews” from the menu.\r\nFind the review you want to respond to and click \"Reply.\"\r\nCraft a polite and professional response, whether the review is positive or negative.\r\n23. Can I remove negative reviews from my Google Business Profile?\r\nYou cannot directly remove reviews, but you can report reviews that violate Google’s review policies (e.g., spam, offensive content, or false information). Google will investigate and may remove the review if it’s found to be in violation.\r\n\r\n24. How do reviews impact my local search ranking?\r\nReviews are a significant ranking factor for local SEO. Businesses with a higher volume of positive reviews tend to rank higher in the Local Pack and Maps results. Google considers the quantity, quality, and recency of reviews when determining rankings.\r\n\r\n25. Should I respond to negative reviews on Google Business Profile?\r\nYes, responding to negative reviews is important. A thoughtful and professional response can demonstrate that you value customer feedback and are willing to resolve issues. This can help mitigate the impact of a negative review and even encourage the reviewer to update their rating.\r\n\r\nAdvanced Features of Google Business Profile\r\n26. What are Google Business Profile Insights?\r\nGBP Insights provide data on how customers find your business and interact with your profile. You can see:\r\n\r\nHow many people searched for your business directly or found it through a general category or keyword search.\r\nWhere customers view your profile (Google Search or Maps).\r\nActions taken by customers, like website visits, calls, and direction requests.\r\nCustomer demographics and peak times for foot traffic.\r\n27. How do I set up messaging on Google Business Profile?\r\nMessaging allows customers to send you direct messages from your profile. To enable it:\r\n\r\nSign in to your GBP account.\r\nClick on “Messaging” in the menu.\r\nTurn on messaging and set up automated responses, if desired.\r\nCustomers can now message you directly from your Google listing.\r\n28. What is the Q&A section on Google Business Profile?\r\nThe Q&A section allows users to ask questions about your business, which you (or other customers) can answer. This is\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nChatGPT said:\r\nChatGPT\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nGoogle Ads general questions\r\n1. What is Google Ads?\r\nGoogle Ads is an online advertising platform developed by Google where advertisers bid to display ads, service offerings, or videos to web users. It can show ads on Google Search, YouTube, and across the Google Display Network.\r\n\r\n2. How does Google Ads work?\r\nGoogle Ads works on a pay-per-click (PPC) model, where advertisers pay when users click on their ads. Advertisers set a budget, create ad campaigns, and Google displays these ads based on keywords, demographics, and other targeting criteria.\r\n\r\n3. What is Quality Score in Google Ads?\r\nQuality Score is a metric that Google uses to determine the relevance and quality of your ads. It is based on factors like click-through rate (CTR), ad relevance, and landing page experience.\r\n\r\n4. What are keywords in Google Ads?\r\nKeywords are specific words or phrases that describe your product or service. When users search for these terms on Google, your ads can be triggered to appear if the keywords match.\r\n\r\n5. What is a campaign in Google Ads?\r\nA campaign in Google Ads is a series of ad groups with related goals. Campaigns allow you to organize your ads by targeting, budget, and other settings.\r\n\r\nCosts and Budgeting\r\n6. How much does Google Ads cost?\r\nThe cost of Google Ads depends on your industry, competition, and bidding strategy. You can control the cost through daily budgets and bids for each keyword or ad placement.\r\n\r\n7. What is CPC (Cost Per Click)?\r\nCPC is the amount you pay when a user clicks on your ad. It can vary based on the competition for the keyword and your Quality Score.\r\n\r\n8. What is CPM (Cost Per Mille)?\r\nCPM refers to the cost per thousand impressions. It’s a bidding model where you pay based on how many times your ad is shown, rather than clicks.\r\n\r\n9. What is daily budget in Google Ads?\r\nThe daily budget is the amount you\'re willing to spend on your ads per day. Google will try to distribute your spending evenly over time, but some days you might spend more or less.\r\n\r\n10. Can I run Google Ads with a small budget?\r\nYes, you can run ads with a small budget. The key is to optimize your campaigns to focus on the most relevant and cost-effective keywords and audiences.\r\n\r\nTargeting and Audiences\r\n11. What is audience targeting in Google Ads?\r\nAudience targeting allows you to reach users based on demographics, interests, behaviors, and more. You can choose to target specific age groups, locations, or people who have visited your site (remarketing).\r\n\r\n12. What are negative keywords in Google Ads?\r\nNegative keywords prevent your ads from being shown for certain searches. This helps refine your audience and avoid irrelevant clicks.\r\n\r\n13. How does geo-targeting work in Google Ads?\r\nGeo-targeting lets you show your ads to users in specific locations, whether by country, region, or even within a certain radius around your business.\r\n\r\n14. What is remarketing in Google Ads?\r\nRemarketing allows you to show ads to users who have previously visited your website. It’s a way to re-engage potential customers who didn’t convert on their first visit.\r\n\r\n15. What is dynamic search ads (DSA)?\r\nDynamic Search Ads automatically create ads based on the content of your website. Google matches relevant search queries to your site’s content, generating ad headlines and landing pages dynamically.\r\n\r\nPerformance and Metrics\r\n16. How can I track the performance of my Google Ads campaigns?\r\nYou can track performance through Google Ads metrics like impressions, clicks, click-through rate (CTR), conversions, and cost-per-conversion. Google Ads also integrates with Google Analytics for deeper insights.\r\n\r\n17. What is conversion tracking in Google Ads?\r\nConversion tracking is a tool that helps you measure when users complete a specific action on your site after clicking on your ad, such as a purchase, sign-up, or form submission.\r\n\r\n18. What is the click-through rate (CTR)?\r\nCTR is the percentage of people who clicked on your ad compared to the number of impressions it received. A higher CTR indicates that your ad is more appealing to users.\r\n\r\n19. What is ad rank in Google Ads?\r\nAd Rank is Google’s metric for determining the position of your ad in search results. It’s based on your bid, Quality Score, and expected impact of ad extensions and other factors.\r\n\r\n20. How can I improve my Google Ads performance?\r\nTo improve performance, you can:\r\n\r\nOptimize your keywords and ads based on performance data.\r\nUse negative keywords to filter out irrelevant traffic.\r\nAdjust your bidding strategy to get more conversions.\r\nTest different ad copy and landing pages.\r\nImprove your Quality Score by enhancing ad relevance and user experience.\r\nAd Formats and Extensions\r\n21. What ad formats are available in Google Ads?\r\nGoogle Ads offers various ad formats, including:\r\n\r\nSearch Ads: Text ads displayed on Google search results.\r\nDisplay Ads: Visual banner ads shown across the Google Display Network.\r\nVideo Ads: Ads shown on YouTube.\r\nShopping Ads: Ads showcasing products with prices and images.\r\nApp Promotion Ads: Ads promoting mobile apps.\r\n22. What are ad extensions?\r\nAd extensions are additional pieces of information that can be added to your ads, such as phone numbers, location, site links, and callouts. They help improve the visibility and effectiveness of ads.\r\n\r\n23. What are responsive search ads (RSA)?\r\nResponsive Search Ads automatically adjust headlines and descriptions based on what is likely to perform best for the user’s query. You provide multiple headlines and descriptions, and Google tests combinations to find the most effective.\r\n\r\n24. What are Google Shopping Ads?\r\nGoogle Shopping Ads display product listings, including images, prices, and store details. They appear when users search for specific products on Google.\r\n\r\nGoogle Ads Policies\r\n25. What are the main Google Ads policies?\r\nGoogle Ads has strict policies regarding content, including:\r\n\r\nProhibited content (e.g., dangerous products, hate speech, misleading claims).\r\nProhibited practices (e.g., data collection without user consent).\r\nRestricted content (e.g., alcohol, gambling, healthcare products). Ads that violate these policies may be disapproved or lead to account suspension.\r\n26. Can my Google Ads account be suspended?\r\nYes, accounts can be suspended for violating Google’s policies, such as repeated ad disapprovals, suspicious payment activity, or promoting prohibited content.\r\n\r\nThese questions cover various aspects of Google Ads, from the basics to more advanced topics. Let me know if you need further details on any of these!\r\n27. What are bidding strategies in Google Ads?\r\nBidding strategies determine how you pay for clicks, impressions, or conversions in Google Ads. Some common bidding strategies include:\r\n\r\nManual CPC (Cost-Per-Click): You set bids for individual keywords.\r\nEnhanced CPC: Google adjusts your manual bids to maximize conversions.\r\nTarget CPA (Cost-Per-Acquisition): Google sets bids to help get as many conversions as possible at the set cost per acquisition.\r\nTarget ROAS (Return on Ad Spend): Google sets bids to maximize revenue based on your return on ad spend target.\r\nMaximize Conversions: Automatically sets bids to get the most conversions within your budget.\r\nMaximize Clicks: Automatically sets bids to get the most clicks within your budget.\r\n28. What is automated bidding in Google Ads?\r\nAutomated bidding uses machine learning to automatically set bids for your ads based on campaign goals. Google adjusts bids in real-time based on various factors like device, location, time of day, and user behavior to optimize for conversions or clicks.\r\n\r\n29. What is smart bidding in Google Ads?\r\nSmart Bidding is a subset of automated bidding strategies that optimize for conversions or conversion value using advanced machine learning. Examples include Target CPA, Target ROAS, and Maximize Conversions.\r\n\r\n30. What is Target CPA (Cost Per Acquisition)?\r\nTarget CPA is a bidding strategy where Google aims to get you as many conversions as possible at or below a specified cost per acquisition. It’s helpful for advertisers focused on generating leads or sales.\r\n\r\n31. What is Target ROAS (Return on Ad Spend)?\r\nTarget ROAS is a bidding strategy where Google aims to maximize revenue while maintaining a specific return on ad spend. For example, if your target ROAS is 400%, Google will aim to generate $4 in revenue for every $1 spent.\r\n\r\nAdvanced Targeting Options\r\n32. What is demographic targeting in Google Ads?\r\nDemographic targeting allows you to target users based on their age, gender, household income, and parental status. This is useful for tailoring ads to specific audience segments that are most likely to convert.\r\n\r\n33. What is affinity audience targeting?\r\nAffinity audience targeting allows you to show your ads to people based on their long-term interests and habits. Google segments users based on their browsing behavior and preferences to place them in predefined categories like \"Travel Enthusiasts\" or \"Foodies.\"\r\n\r\n34. What is in-market audience targeting?\r\nIn-market audience targeting allows you to reach users who are actively considering purchasing a product or service in a specific category. Google identifies these users based on their recent search and browsing behaviors.\r\n\r\n35. What is custom intent audience targeting?\r\nCustom intent audiences allow you to create your own audience segments based on the specific keywords and websites your ideal customers are searching for and visiting.\r\n\r\n36. What is location targeting in Google Ads?\r\nLocation targeting allows you to show your ads to people in specific geographic locations. You can target by country, state, city, postal code, or a specific radius around a location. This helps ensure your ads are only shown to relevant users in your desired area.\r\n\r\nGoogle Ads Tools\r\n37. What is the Google Ads Keyword Planner?\r\nThe Keyword Planner is a tool that helps you find new keyword ideas and get search volume estimates for keywords. It also provides estimates for keyword costs, helping you make informed decisions about your bidding strategies.\r\n\r\n38. What is Google Ads Editor?\r\nGoogle Ads Editor is a downloadable application that allows you to manage your Google Ads campaigns offline. You can make bulk edits to campaigns, ads, and keywords, then upload the changes when you’re back online.\r\n\r\n39. What is the Google Ads Performance Planner?\r\nThe Performance Planner is a tool that helps you forecast the potential performance of your campaigns by adjusting factors like budget and bidding strategies. It allows you to simulate how changes could affect metrics like conversions and clicks.\r\n\r\n40. What is Google Tag Manager?\r\nGoogle Tag Manager is a tool that allows you to manage and deploy marketing tags (snippets of code or tracking pixels) on your website without having to modify the code. It’s especially useful for implementing Google Ads conversion tracking and remarketing.\r\n\r\n41. What is Google Analytics?\r\nGoogle Analytics is a web analytics service that tracks and reports website traffic. When integrated with Google Ads, it provides insights into how users interact with your website after clicking on your ads, allowing you to track conversions, behavior, and more.\r\n\r\nGoogle Ads Optimizations\r\n42. How do I use A/B testing in Google Ads?\r\nA/B testing (also known as split testing) involves creating two or more versions of your ads, changing a single variable like ad copy or call-to-action, and running them simultaneously. This helps you determine which version performs better and refine your ads accordingly.\r\n\r\n43. What is ad scheduling in Google Ads?\r\nAd scheduling (also known as dayparting) allows you to choose specific days or times when your ads will appear. This can be useful if your business operates during certain hours or if your target audience is more active at specific times.\r\n\r\n44. How can I optimize my landing page for Google Ads?\r\nTo optimize your landing page, ensure it is relevant to the ad, loads quickly, and provides a seamless user experience. Focus on the following:\r\n\r\nUse compelling headlines and content that match the ad.\r\nEnsure the page is mobile-friendly.\r\nHave a clear and concise call-to-action (CTA).\r\nReduce load time for better user experience and Quality Score.\r\nImplement conversion tracking to measure performance.\r\n45. How do I improve my ad relevance?\r\nAd relevance refers to how closely your ad matches the user\'s search query or intent. You can improve ad relevance by:\r\n\r\nUsing targeted keywords in your ad copy.\r\nMatching your ad copy to the user’s search intent.\r\nCreating tightly themed ad groups with focused keywords.\r\nRegularly updating your ads based on performance data.\r\nGoogle Ads Account Structure\r\n46. How should I structure my Google Ads account?\r\nA well-structured Google Ads account improves performance and management. Common practices include:\r\n\r\nCampaigns: Group campaigns by goals (e.g., brand awareness, lead generation).\r\nAd Groups: Each campaign can have multiple ad groups, each focused on specific keywords.\r\nKeywords: Use targeted and specific keywords for each ad group.\r\nAds: Create variations of ad copy within each ad group for testing.\r\n47. What is an ad group in Google Ads?\r\nAn ad group contains one or more ads and a set of related keywords. Each ad group within a campaign focuses on a specific theme or product, allowing for more targeted and relevant ads.\r\n\r\n48. How do I use keyword match types in Google Ads?\r\nKeyword match types determine how closely a user\'s search query must match your keyword for your ad to show. There are four main types:\r\n\r\nBroad Match: Your ad can show for searches that include misspellings, synonyms, and related searches.\r\nBroad Match Modifier: Ads only show when the search includes the exact words in your keyword, but in any order.\r\nPhrase Match: Ads appear for searches that match your keyword phrase exactly, but may include additional words before or after.\r\nExact Match: Ads show only when the search query matches your keyword exactly.\r\n\r\n\r\nHere are even more advanced questions and answers about Google Ads, covering specialized topics, troubleshooting, and more strategic insights:\r\n\r\nAdvanced Campaign Strategies\r\n49. What is a Smart Campaign in Google Ads?\r\nA Smart Campaign is a simplified, automated campaign type where Google handles most of the heavy lifting. It\'s designed for small businesses and focuses on driving conversions or calls without the need for advanced management. You provide some inputs (like your business goals and budget), and Google optimizes the rest.\r\n\r\n50. What are Shopping Campaigns in Google Ads?\r\nShopping campaigns are designed for e-commerce businesses and promote products through Shopping Ads. These ads appear in Google Search results and the Google Shopping tab with product images, prices, and store names. They are based on your product feed from Google Merchant Center.\r\n\r\n51. What is Google Discovery Ads?\r\nDiscovery Ads appear in Google’s Discover feed, YouTube, and Gmail. These visually rich ads target users based on their interests and behaviors, helping you reach new potential customers who are not actively searching for your products but are likely to engage.\r\n\r\n52. What is a Performance Max campaign?\r\nPerformance Max is a goal-based campaign type that allows advertisers to access all of Google Ads inventory from a single campaign. It uses automation to deliver ads across Search, YouTube, Display, Discover, Gmail, and Maps to maximize conversions or conversion value.\r\n\r\n53. What is responsive display advertising?\r\nResponsive display ads automatically adjust their size, appearance, and format to fit available ad spaces. You upload images, headlines, logos, and descriptions, and Google creates the ad combinations that perform best across the Google Display Network.\r\n\r\nTroubleshooting Google Ads Issues\r\n54. Why are my Google Ads not showing?\r\nThere are several reasons your ads might not be showing:\r\n\r\nLow budget: Your daily budget may be too low to compete in the auction.\r\nLow Ad Rank: Your Ad Rank may be too low because of a poor bid or low Quality Score.\r\nAd disapproval: Your ads may have been disapproved for policy violations.\r\nKeyword issues: You may be using negative keywords or targeting overly specific match types that limit visibility.\r\nTargeting settings: Your audience or geographic targeting may be too narrow.\r\nCampaign status: Ensure your campaign is not paused or has ended.\r\n55. What to do if my Google Ads are disapproved?\r\nIf your ads are disapproved, review the disapproval reason in your Google Ads account. Google provides information on which policies were violated. Common fixes include adjusting ad copy, resolving issues with landing pages, or clarifying product claims.\r\n\r\n56. Why is my click-through rate (CTR) low?\r\nA low CTR can result from several factors:\r\n\r\nIrrelevant ad copy: Ensure your ad matches the user’s intent and is compelling.\r\nPoor targeting: Make sure your keywords or audiences are correctly targeted.\r\nLow-quality ad creative: Improve your headlines and descriptions to grab attention.\r\nAd rank: Low Ad Rank can reduce your ad’s position, decreasing its visibility and CTR.\r\n57. What is the reason for high CPC in Google Ads?\r\nHigh CPCs can occur due to:\r\n\r\nCompetitive keywords: Keywords in high-demand industries (like insurance or finance) tend to have higher CPCs.\r\nLow Quality Score: Poor ad relevance or landing page experience can drive up costs.\r\nBidding strategy: An aggressive bidding strategy like Maximize Clicks can increase CPCs.\r\nAccount Management and Organization\r\n58. How do I create a Google Ads MCC (My Client Center) account?\r\nAn MCC account (now known as a Manager Account) is a tool for managing multiple Google Ads accounts from a single dashboard. To create an MCC account:\r\n\r\nGo to the Google Ads Manager Account page.\r\nClick \"Create a manager account.\"\r\nFollow the prompts to create your account.\r\nOnce set up, you can link existing accounts or create new ones under your MCC.\r\n59. What is ad rotation in Google Ads?\r\nAd rotation refers to how Google delivers multiple ads within the same ad group. There are two main settings:\r\n\r\nOptimize: Google prioritizes ads that are expected to perform better based on historical data.\r\nDo not optimize (rotate indefinitely): Ads are rotated evenly regardless of performance.\r\n60. How do I pause or remove a Google Ads campaign?\r\nTo pause a campaign, go to the Campaigns tab, find the campaign you want to pause, click on the status column, and select “Pause.”\r\nTo remove a campaign, follow the same steps but select “Remove.” Pausing retains historical data, whereas removing will archive the campaign, although data will still be accessible.\r\n61. How do I set up conversion tracking in Google Ads?\r\nConversion tracking allows you to measure when users complete desired actions after clicking your ad. Here\'s how to set it up:\r\n\r\nSign in to your Google Ads account and go to the \"Tools & Settings\" menu.\r\nUnder \"Measurement,\" click on \"Conversions.\"\r\nClick the \"+\" button and choose the type of conversion (website, app, phone calls, etc.).\r\nFollow the prompts to create your conversion action and generate a tracking code.\r\nAdd the tracking code to your website or integrate it through Google Tag Manager.\r\n62. What is cross-account conversion tracking?\r\nCross-account conversion tracking allows you to track conversions across multiple Google Ads accounts from a single conversion tag. It is particularly useful for agencies or businesses managing multiple domains or ad accounts.\r\n\r\nGoogle Ads Policies and Compliance\r\n63. What is the Google Ads policy on sensitive events?\r\nGoogle Ads restricts ads that attempt to capitalize on sensitive events like natural disasters, global pandemics, or political unrest. Ads related to these events must be handled with care, focusing on providing useful information rather than exploiting the situation.\r\n\r\n64. What are Google Ads restrictions on healthcare and medicines?\r\nGoogle has strict policies regarding the promotion of healthcare products and services, including:\r\n\r\nPrescription medications: Ads for prescription drugs are allowed in specific countries and must meet local laws.\r\nOver-the-counter drugs: These ads are restricted and must comply with Google\'s local requirements.\r\nHealthcare-related services: Ads promoting healthcare services (such as telemedicine) must be pre-approved and comply with advertising regulations.\r\n65. What are the rules around alcohol advertising in Google Ads?\r\nGoogle allows the promotion of alcohol-related content but with restrictions:\r\n\r\nTargeting: Ads must target users above the legal drinking age in their country.\r\nCompliance: Ads must follow local laws and advertising standards regarding alcohol promotion.\r\nContent: The ads must not promote excessive consumption, drinking games, or glamorize alcohol.\r\nGoogle Ads and Third-Party Tools\r\n66. How does Google Ads integrate with Google Analytics?\r\nBy linking your Google Ads account to Google Analytics, you can track user interactions across your website and analyze behavior beyond conversions. It helps to:\r\n\r\nMeasure user activity (like time on site or pages per session) after clicking on ads.\r\nSegment traffic by campaigns, keywords, or ads to optimize performance.\r\nView conversion paths to understand how users engage with your site before converting.\r\n67. What is Google Merchant Center?\r\nGoogle Merchant Center is a platform where businesses can upload product information that is used in Shopping Ads. It’s essential for running Google Shopping campaigns as it feeds product data to Google, including prices, availability, and descriptions.\r\n\r\n68. What are third-party tools that can help optimize Google Ads?\r\nSome third-party tools can help with advanced Google Ads management, including:\r\n\r\nSEMRush: For keyword research and competitive analysis.\r\nOptmyzr: For automating bid adjustments and managing ad scripts.\r\nWordStream: For campaign analysis and recommendations.\r\nUnbounce: For creating optimized landing pages.\r\nSpyFu: For competitor research and keyword spying.\r\n69. How do I use scripts in Google Ads?\r\nGoogle Ads Scripts allow for automated campaign management by writing JavaScript code to automate tasks. Scripts can be used for things like:\r\n\r\nPausing underperforming keywords.\r\nAdjusting bids based on time of day.\r\nAutomatically generating reports. You can find pre-built scripts or create custom ones based on your specific needs.\r\n\r\nGoogle Ads Reporting and Analytics\r\n70. What is the difference between Google Ads and Google Analytics data?\r\nGoogle Ads tracks clicks, impressions, and conversions directly from your ads, while Google Analytics tracks user behavior on your website. The key differences include:\r\n\r\nAttribution window: Google Ads may attribute conversions differently based on the attribution model you choose (e.g., last-click or time-decay), whereas Google Analytics uses its own multi-channel funnel model.\r\nData delay: Google Ads data updates more frequently than Google Analytics, which may have a slight delay in reporting.\r\nUser actions: Google Ads focuses on ad interactions, while Google Analytics provides deeper insights into user behavior (time on site, pages per session, etc.).\r\n71. What are custom reports in Google Ads?\r\nCustom reports allow you to create tailored data views based on the metrics that matter most to your campaign goals. You can:\r\n\r\nFilter for specific performance data like conversion rates, CTR, or ROI.\r\nSegment by devices, locations, and audiences.\r\nSave the custom report for future use or share it with team members.\r\n72. What is the Search Terms Report in Google Ads?\r\nThe Search Terms Report shows the actual search queries that triggered your ads. This helps you understand:\r\n\r\nWhich terms are driving clicks and conversions.\r\nIdentify irrelevant or underperforming terms to add as negative keywords.\r\nDiscover new, high-performing keywords that you may want to bid on.\r\n73. What are the key performance indicators (KPIs) in Google Ads?\r\nThe key KPIs in Google Ads depend on your campaign goals but typically include:\r\n\r\nClick-Through Rate (CTR): Measures the percentage of people who clicked on your ad.\r\nConversion Rate: The percentage of clicks that resulted in conversions.\r\nCost-Per-Click (CPC): How much you’re paying for each click.\r\nCost-Per-Acquisition (CPA): The average cost of generating one conversion.\r\nReturn on Ad Spend (ROAS): The revenue you earn for every dollar spent on ads.\r\nAdvanced Targeting Techniques\r\n74. What is remarketing in Google Ads?\r\nRemarketing allows you to target users who have already visited your website but did not convert. This is done by:\r\n\r\nCreating lists based on specific actions users took (e.g., visiting a certain page or adding a product to their cart).\r\nServing ads to these users as they browse other websites or use Google Search. Remarketing is highly effective for bringing back potential customers and encouraging them to complete their purchase or other desired actions.\r\n75. What are remarketing lists for search ads (RLSA)?\r\nRLSA is a feature that lets you customize search ads for people who have previously visited your website. You can:\r\n\r\nAdjust bids for these users, for example, bidding higher for users who visited specific product pages.\r\nShow tailored ads with messaging designed for returning visitors, like offering discounts or highlighting new products.\r\n76. What are custom affinity audiences?\r\nCustom affinity audiences allow you to create a more tailored audience based on your business goals. You can define these audiences by:\r\n\r\nInterests: Choose interests that align with your target customer.\r\nURLs: Include websites that your target audience might visit.\r\nPlaces: Specify locations that your audience might frequent. This gives you more control over targeting than Google\'s predefined affinity audience segments.\r\n77. What are custom intent audiences?\r\nCustom intent audiences allow you to target people based on their most recent purchase intent or activity. You can create these audiences by specifying:\r\n\r\nKeywords: Users who have searched for or are interested in specific keywords.\r\nURLs: People who have visited certain websites related to your business or product. Custom intent audiences are often used in display campaigns to target users more likely to be interested in purchasing.\r\n78. What is demographic targeting exclusion in Google Ads?\r\nDemographic targeting exclusion allows you to exclude specific demographic groups from seeing your ads. For instance, you can exclude users of a certain age range, gender, or income bracket if they are unlikely to convert based on your data.\r\n\r\n79. What are life events in Google Ads targeting?\r\nGoogle Ads allows you to target users based on major life events like getting married, moving, or having a baby. This type of targeting can be particularly useful for advertisers whose products or services are relevant during these life transitions.\r\n\r\nGoogle Ads Automation\r\n80. What is Google Ads automated rules?\r\nAutomated rules in Google Ads allow you to create custom rules to automatically make changes to your campaigns. For example, you can set rules to:\r\n\r\nPause underperforming ads.\r\nAdjust bids based on performance.\r\nChange budgets at specific times of the day. Automated rules help streamline account management and reduce manual work.\r\n81. What is automated ad creative optimization in Google Ads?\r\nAutomated ad creative optimization uses machine learning to determine which combinations of headlines, descriptions, and visuals perform best. Google automatically tests different variations of your ads and serves the most effective combinations to maximize performance.\r\n\r\n82. How do I use responsive search ads?\r\nResponsive search ads allow you to provide multiple headlines and descriptions, and Google will dynamically test different combinations. You can:\r\n\r\nEnter up to 15 headlines and 4 descriptions.\r\nGoogle’s machine learning will test these combinations to find the most effective ad for each search query.\r\nThis increases the likelihood of your ad appearing for relevant searches and improving performance over time.\r\n83. What is Google Ads automated bid adjustment?\r\nGoogle Ads automated bid adjustment uses machine learning to change bids based on the likelihood of a conversion. Bid adjustments are applied in real-time and take into account factors like:\r\n\r\nUser location.\r\nDevice type.\r\nTime of day.\r\nUser behavior and search intent. This helps optimize your bids to get the best possible results within your budget.\r\nIndustry-Specific Google Ads Strategies\r\n84. How do I use Google Ads for local businesses?\r\nLocal businesses can use Google Ads effectively by:\r\n\r\nLocation targeting: Set up campaigns that target specific geographic areas where your customers are located.\r\nCall extensions: Encourage users to call your business directly from your ads.\r\nLocal search ads: Use ads in Google Maps to show your business at the top of local search results.\r\nLocation extensions: Show your address and phone number in the ad copy to attract local customers.\r\n85. How do e-commerce businesses succeed with Google Ads?\r\nE-commerce businesses can thrive on Google Ads by:\r\n\r\nUsing Shopping Ads: Display your products directly in Google Search results with price, images, and product details.\r\nDynamic Remarketing: Show personalized ads with products that users viewed or added to their cart but didn’t purchase.\r\nConversion tracking: Set up robust conversion tracking to measure sales and optimize campaigns based on revenue, not just clicks.\r\nSeasonal campaigns: Launch campaigns around holidays, sales events, or product launches to capitalize on high purchase intent.\r\n86. How can SaaS companies use Google Ads effectively?\r\nSaaS companies can drive leads and subscriptions with Google Ads by:\r\n\r\nTargeting relevant keywords: Focus on search terms that users would use when researching software solutions.\r\nUsing lead forms: Google Ads’ lead form extensions allow users to submit their information without leaving the search results page.\r\nFree trials or demos: Advertise offers like free trials or demos to entice potential customers to sign up and experience the product.\r\n87. How can service-based businesses use Google Ads?\r\nService-based businesses (plumbers, lawyers, consultants) can:\r\n\r\nTarget local customers: Use location-based targeting to reach people looking for services in their area.\r\nUse call-only ads: These ads focus on driving phone calls instead of clicks to a website.\r\nShowcase testimonials: Include customer reviews and testimonials in ad copy to build trust with potential clients.\r\nUse appointment booking extensions: Allow users to book appointments directly from your ad.\r\nCompetitor Strategies in Google Ads\r\n88. How do I use competitor keywords in Google Ads?\r\nYou can bid on competitor brand names and keywords to attract users who are considering your competitors. However, there are some best practices:\r\n\r\nAvoid using competitor names in ad copy: This can lead to policy violations and lower Quality Scores.\r\nProvide compelling offers: Ensure your ads highlight why your business is a better alternative, whether through pricing, features, or customer service.\r\nMonitor Quality Score: Bidding on competitor terms can sometimes result in lower Quality Scores if your ad is not directly relevant to the search intent.\r\n89. What is competitive analysis in Google Ads?\r\nCompetitive analysis in Google Ads involves using tools to monitor what keywords, ads, and landing pages your competitors are using. Tools like SEMrush, SpyFu, or the Auction Insights Report in Google Ads can help you:\r\n\r\nIdentify high-performing competitor keywords.\r\nSee how often your competitors’ ads appear in auctions alongside yours.\r\nDiscover bidding strategies and gaps in your own keyword strategy.\r\n90. What is the Auction Insights Report in Google Ads?\r\nThe Auction Insights Report shows how your ads are performing compared to competitors who are participating in the same auctions. You can see:\r\n\r\nImpression share: How often your ad is appearing versus competitors.\r\nOverlap rate: How often your ad appears alongside a competitor’s ad.\r\nPosition above rate: How often your ad appears above a competitor’s ad. This data helps you understand your competitive landscape and adjust your bidding and strategy accordingly.\r\n\r\nAdvanced Bidding Strategies\r\n91. What is Enhanced CPC (ECPC) in Google Ads?\r\nEnhanced CPC is a semi-automated bidding strategy that adjusts your manual bids for clicks that are more likely to lead to conversions. Google automatically raises or lowers your bids based on the likelihood of converting, while staying within your overall budget.\r\n\r\n92. What is Target CPA (Cost-Per-Acquisition) bidding?\r\nTarget CPA is a smart bidding strategy where Google automatically sets bids to get as many conversions as possible at your desired cost per acquisition. Google adjusts bids based on various signals like device, location, and time of day to help you meet your target CPA.\r\n\r\n93. What is Target ROAS (Return on Ad Spend) bidding?\r\nTarget ROAS bidding is designed to optimize your campaigns for the highest possible return on ad spend. Google uses machine learning to predict how likely a click is to convert and what value that conversion will bring, then adjusts your bids accordingly to maximize revenue for every dollar spent.\r\n\r\n94. How does Maximize Conversions bidding work?\r\nMaximize Conversions is an automated bidding strategy that aims to get the most conversions within your daily budget. Google Ads optimizes bids using machine learning to prioritize users who are more likely to convert, regardless of individual keyword bids.\r\n\r\n95. What is the Maximize Conversion Value bidding strategy?\r\nThis strategy focuses on maximizing the overall value of conversions rather than the number of conversions. It’s ideal for businesses that assign different values to different types of conversions (like high-value products versus low-value ones).\r\n\r\nConversion Tracking and Attribution Models\r\n96. What is Google Ads conversion tracking?\r\nConversion tracking measures the actions users take after interacting with your ad, such as making a purchase, filling out a form, or calling your business. To set it up, you need to:\r\n\r\nDefine what a conversion is for your business.\r\nInstall a conversion tracking tag on your website or integrate it with Google Tag Manager.\r\nAnalyze conversions in your Google Ads account to optimize for better performance.\r\n97. What are Google Ads attribution models?\r\nAttribution models determine how credit for conversions is assigned across different interactions with your ads. The main models include:\r\n\r\nLast click: All credit goes to the last ad clicked.\r\nFirst click: All credit goes to the first ad clicked.\r\nLinear: Equal credit is given to all clicks leading to the conversion.\r\nTime decay: More credit is given to clicks closer to the time of conversion.\r\nPosition-based: 40% of credit goes to the first and last clicks, and 20% is spread across the middle interactions.\r\nData-driven: Google’s machine learning model attributes credit based on actual performance data.\r\n98. How do I use offline conversion tracking in Google Ads?\r\nOffline conversion tracking allows you to track when online leads (like form submissions) turn into offline sales or actions (like phone calls or in-person visits). To use it, you need:\r\n\r\nA system to track leads, like a CRM.\r\nIntegration with Google Ads to upload conversion data.\r\nOffline conversions can be tracked by importing data manually or using Google Ads API.\r\n99. What is conversion lag in Google Ads?\r\nConversion lag refers to the delay between when a click happens and when a conversion is recorded. This delay is common in industries with longer sales cycles or where users may take time to complete actions. Google Ads provides data on estimated conversion lag in your reports.\r\n\r\n100. What is view-through conversion tracking?\r\nView-through conversions track when a user sees but doesn’t click your ad, then later converts through a different action (like a direct visit to your website). This is especially useful for display and video ads where users might not immediately click but still remember your brand.\r\n\r\nOptimization and Scaling Tactics\r\n101. What are SKAGs (Single Keyword Ad Groups)?\r\nSKAGs are a Google Ads strategy where each ad group is focused on a single keyword. This allows for:\r\n\r\nHighly relevant ad copy.\r\nMore precise bidding strategies.\r\nBetter Quality Scores due to increased ad relevance. While effective, managing SKAGs at scale can be time-consuming, so automation tools may be helpful.\r\n102. How can I use A/B testing in Google Ads?\r\nA/B testing in Google Ads involves running experiments to compare the performance of different ad variations. This can include:\r\n\r\nTesting headlines or descriptions.\r\nTrying different landing pages.\r\nExperimenting with bidding strategies. Use Google Ads’ Drafts & Experiments feature to test and measure variations in real-time without disrupting your main campaigns.\r\n103. What are in-market audiences?\r\nIn-market audiences are groups of users that Google identifies as being actively researching or comparing products or services similar to yours. This data is based on user behavior across Google’s platforms, and targeting these users can help reach people closer to making a purchase.\r\n\r\n104. How do I optimize for mobile in Google Ads?\r\nMobile optimization involves ensuring your ads and landing pages are effective on mobile devices. Best practices include:\r\n\r\nCreating mobile-preferred ads.\r\nUsing responsive search and display ads.\r\nEnsuring your website is mobile-friendly and loads quickly.\r\nAdjusting bids for mobile traffic based on performance.\r\n105. What is a good CTR for Google Ads?\r\nA good click-through rate (CTR) depends on the industry, campaign type, and keyword intent. However, the average CTR across all industries in Google Ads is about 2%. High-performing search campaigns can have a CTR of 5% or more, while display ads tend to have lower CTRs around 0.5-1%.\r\n\r\nGoogle Ads and YouTube\r\n106. What are YouTube TrueView ads?\r\nTrueView ads are a YouTube ad format where advertisers only pay when users watch at least 30 seconds of the ad (or the full ad, if it\'s shorter) or interact with the ad (like clicking on a call-to-action). The main types of TrueView ads include:\r\n\r\nIn-stream ads: Skippable ads that play before, during, or after a video.\r\nDiscovery ads: Ads that appear alongside search results or recommended videos.\r\n107. What are bumper ads on YouTube?\r\nBumper ads are non-skippable video ads up to 6 seconds long. These ads are designed for brand awareness and reach, as they are quick, impactful, and shown before videos on YouTube.\r\n\r\n108. How do I measure YouTube ad performance in Google Ads?\r\nYouTube ad performance can be measured through metrics such as:\r\n\r\nView rate: The percentage of users who watched the ad out of those who had the opportunity to view it.\r\nAverage watch time: The average duration users spent watching the video.\r\nCPV (Cost-per-view): How much you’re paying for each view.\r\nConversions: Actions users took after watching the ad, such as visiting your website or making a purchase.\r\n109. What is YouTube masthead advertising?\r\nYouTube Masthead ads are highly visible ads that appear at the top of the YouTube homepage across devices. They are primarily used for massive reach and awareness campaigns, and they are sold on a cost-per-day basis, making them a premium ad option for larger brands.\r\n\r\n110. What is Google Video Partners?\r\nGoogle Video Partners (GVP) are websites and apps that allow Google video ads to be displayed outside of YouTube. This network expands your video ad reach beyond YouTube, offering additional inventory on platforms that support video content.\r\n\r\nBudget Management and Account Structure\r\n111. What is the shared budget feature in Google Ads?\r\nA shared budget allows you to allocate a single daily budget across multiple campaigns in your account. Google then distributes this budget to whichever campaigns are performing best on a given day, helping you maximize the efficiency of your ad spend.\r\n\r\n112. How do I handle budget pacing in Google Ads?\r\nBudget pacing involves managing your daily budget to avoid overspending early in the day or week. To do this:\r\n\r\nMonitor daily performance and adjust bids or budgets as needed.\r\nUse automated rules to change bid amounts or pause campaigns when a certain threshold is reached.\r\nImplement Maximize Conversions or other smart bidding strategies to optimize for performance within your budget.\r\n113. What is account structure optimization?\r\nOptimizing your account structure involves organizing your campaigns and ad groups in a way that maximizes control and performance. Best practices include:\r\n\r\nGrouping similar keywords into tightly themed ad groups.\r\nCreating separate campaigns for different product lines, locations, or audiences.\r\nUsing clear and descriptive naming conventions to easily manage multiple campaigns.\r\nSplitting campaigns by device or geography if performance differs significantly across these factors.\r\n114. How do I manage seasonal budget changes in Google Ads?\r\nSeasonal budget changes are common for businesses with fluctuating demand. To adjust your budget:\r\n\r\nIncrease budget during high-demand periods like holidays or sales events.\r\nUse automated rules to increase or decrease budget based on performance or time of year.\r\nMonitor conversion trends and adjust bids to align with seasonal traffic and competition.\r\n115. What is the Google Ads Credit system?\r\nGoogle sometimes offers promotional credits to new advertisers or as part of special promotions. These credits can be applied to your account to cover a portion of your ad spend, allowing you to test out campaigns without a significant upfront investment.\r\n\r\nGoogle Ads for Mobile Apps\r\n116. What are Google App campaigns?\r\nGoogle App campaigns promote mobile apps across Google’s vast network, including Search, YouTube, Play Store, and Google Display Network. Google automatically optimizes ads for installs, in-app actions, or engagement, based on the goal you set.\r\n\r\n117. How do I measure app install conversions in Google Ads?\r\nApp install conversions can be measured by integrating with a mobile measurement partner (MMP) or using Firebase, Google\'s app analytics tool. You can track:\r\n\r\nApp installs.\r\nIn-app purchases.\r\nUser retention and engagement metrics.\r\n118. What is Google Play Referrer API?\r\nGoogle Play Referrer API allows you to track and attribute app installs to specific ad campaigns. It helps determine how users found and installed your app, allowing for more accurate reporting on which campaigns are driving the most installs.\r\n\r\nIt looks like we\'ve covered the vast majority of topics related to Google Ads, including advanced strategies, optimization techniques, and industry-specific approaches. Below are some additional niche and future-oriented topics that may still be of interest:\r\n\r\nEmerging Trends in Google Ads\r\n119. How is AI impacting Google Ads?\r\nAI is becoming more integral to Google Ads through:\r\n\r\nSmart bidding: Automatically adjusts bids based on real-time data like device, location, and time of day.\r\nResponsive ads: Uses machine learning to test combinations of headlines, descriptions, and visuals to find the most effective variations.\r\nAudience targeting: Google uses AI to better understand user intent and behavior, allowing advertisers to target users more effectively.\r\nPerformance Max campaigns: This relatively new feature uses AI to optimize across all Google Ads inventory (search, display, YouTube, Gmail, etc.) for maximum conversions.\r\n120. What is Performance Max in Google Ads?\r\nPerformance Max campaigns allow you to run a single campaign across all of Google’s ad networks (Search, Display, YouTube, Gmail, Discover, etc.). These campaigns leverage automation for bidding, budget allocation, audience targeting, and creative optimization. You simply provide assets (like text, images, and videos), and Google’s AI optimizes the delivery of your ads.\r\n\r\n121. What is the role of machine learning in Google Ads?\r\nMachine learning in Google Ads helps:\r\n\r\nOptimize bidding: Adjusting bids based on real-time signals (e.g., user behavior, device, time).\r\nImprove ad relevance: Tailoring ads to match the user’s search intent.\r\nEnhance audience targeting: Automatically identifying high-converting audiences using user data.\r\nPredict performance: Helping advertisers forecast potential results and make informed decisions.\r\nData Privacy and Google Ads\r\n122. How is Google Ads affected by data privacy laws like GDPR and CCPA?\r\nGoogle Ads has had to comply with various data privacy regulations such as GDPR (in Europe) and CCPA (in California). This affects:\r\n\r\nAudience targeting: Users must consent to data collection, which impacts remarketing and audience segments.\r\nTransparency: Google provides users with more information about how their data is used for ad targeting.\r\nConsent requirements: Advertisers are responsible for obtaining proper consent when using tracking technologies like cookies or collecting personal data.\r\n123. What is Google\'s Ads Data Hub?\r\nGoogle Ads Data Hub is a privacy-safe platform for analyzing user data while ensuring that personally identifiable information (PII) remains protected. It allows advertisers to:\r\n\r\nAnalyze cross-channel data for insights into user behavior.\r\nCustomize reports without compromising user privacy.\r\nAccess a more detailed understanding of audience behavior without directly handling sensitive data.\r\n124. How does Google’s FLoC (Federated Learning of Cohorts) impact Google Ads?\r\nFLoC is part of Google\'s plan to phase out third-party cookies in favor of a more privacy-centric model. Instead of tracking individual users, FLoC groups users into \"cohorts\" based on similar browsing behaviors. Google Ads will target these cohorts instead of individuals, ensuring user privacy while still allowing for behavioral targeting.\r\n\r\nGoogle Ads and Other Platforms\r\n125. How do I integrate Google Ads with Google Analytics 4 (GA4)?\r\nGA4 is Google’s new analytics platform designed to track users across websites and apps. Integrating GA4 with Google Ads offers benefits like:\r\n\r\nCross-device tracking: See how users interact with your ads across multiple devices and platforms.\r\nEnhanced audience building: Use Analytics data to create more detailed audience segments for Google Ads targeting.\r\nDeeper attribution insights: Understand user journeys more accurately by combining Analytics and Ads data.\r\n126. How does Google Ads integrate with Salesforce?\r\nIntegrating Google Ads with Salesforce allows businesses to track the full customer journey from click to sale. Key benefits include:\r\n\r\nLead tracking: Automatically import Google Ads leads into Salesforce.\r\nClosed-loop reporting: Measure the ROI of Google Ads campaigns by tracking which leads turn into customers.\r\nAudience targeting: Build Google Ads audiences from your Salesforce CRM data for more precise retargeting.\r\n127. How do I use Google Ads with Shopify?\r\nShopify store owners can use Google Ads through built-in integration tools like Google Channel. This makes it easy to:\r\n\r\nCreate Shopping campaigns: Automatically sync product data with Google Merchant Center.\r\nTrack conversions: Set up conversion tracking to measure purchases made through Google Ads.\r\nOptimize campaigns: Use Google Ads recommendations and reporting to optimize product ads.\r\nVoice Search and Google Ads\r\n128. How does voice search impact Google Ads?\r\nWith the rise of voice search, advertisers need to consider how users are searching differently. Key considerations include:\r\n\r\nLonger keywords: Voice search queries tend to be more conversational and longer than typed queries.\r\nQuestion-based queries: People using voice search often phrase queries as questions (e.g., “Where can I buy running shoes near me?”), so optimizing for question keywords can improve ad performance.\r\nLocal SEO: Voice searches are often local, so optimizing ads for local search intent can drive more foot traffic and conversions.\r\n129. How do I optimize Google Ads for voice search?\r\nTo optimize for voice search, advertisers should:\r\n\r\nUse long-tail keywords that reflect conversational language.\r\nFocus on local targeting and ensure ads appear for \"near me\" searches.\r\nOptimize landing pages for natural language and FAQ-style content.\r\nUse structured data to improve visibility for relevant queries.\r\nNew Formats and Ad Types in Google Ads\r\n130. What are Google Discovery Ads?\r\nDiscovery Ads appear on Google’s Discover feed, YouTube home page, and Gmail promotions tab. They are designed to reach users who are not actively searching but are open to discovering new content or products. Key features include:\r\n\r\nHighly visual, rich media formats.\r\nAutomatically optimized for reach and engagement.\r\nTargeted based on audience insights and intent signals.\r\n131. What are Local Service Ads?\r\nLocal Service Ads are designed for businesses that provide local services (e.g., plumbers, electricians, lawyers). These ads appear at the top of Google Search results with a \"Google Guaranteed\" badge, which increases trust and credibility. Customers can book services directly through the ad, and advertisers only pay for leads (not clicks).\r\n\r\n132. What is Google Gallery Ads?\r\nGallery Ads are a visual ad format that allows advertisers to showcase multiple images in a swipeable carousel format. This type of ad is available on mobile search results and can improve engagement by providing a richer, more interactive experience for users.\r\n\r\n133. What are Smart Shopping campaigns?\r\nSmart Shopping campaigns use machine learning to optimize ad delivery across Google Search, Display, YouTube, and Gmail. They combine standard Shopping ads with remarketing, automatically adjusting bids to maximize conversions or conversion value. Key benefits include:\r\n\r\nReduced need for manual management.\r\nCross-network optimization for greater reach.\r\nSimplified setup, requiring only product data and budget input.\r\nGoogle Ads Best Practices\r\n134. What is ad fatigue in Google Ads, and how do I avoid it?\r\nAd fatigue occurs when users see the same ad too many times, leading to diminishing returns and lower engagement. To avoid ad fatigue:\r\n\r\nRotate ad creatives regularly.\r\nTest different headlines, images, and descriptions.\r\nSet frequency caps to limit how often users see your ads.\r\nUse audience exclusions to prevent showing the same ad to people who have already converted.\r\n135. How do I set up frequency capping in Google Ads?\r\nFrequency capping limits the number of times your ad is shown to the same user over a specific time period (e.g., per day, per week). It’s especially useful in display and video campaigns to prevent oversaturation. Frequency capping can be set up in the campaign settings under the \"Frequency Management\" section.\r\n\r\n136. How do I optimize landing pages for Google Ads?\r\nOptimizing landing pages for Google Ads involves ensuring that they are relevant to the ad copy and provide a seamless experience for users. Key tactics include:\r\n\r\nMatch the message: Ensure the landing page headline and content closely align with the ad.\r\nMobile optimization: Make sure your landing page is fast-loading and responsive on mobile devices.\r\nClear call-to-action (CTA): Have a prominent, easy-to-understand CTA that drives conversions.\r\nA/B testing: Continuously test different versions of your landing page to improve performance.\r\nFuture of Google Ads\r\n137. What is the future of cookie-less advertising in Google Ads?\r\nAs Google phases out third-party cookies, the focus will shift towards more privacy-friendly alternatives like FLoC (Federated Learning of Cohorts), first-party data, and consent-based tracking. Advertisers will need to:\r\n\r\nFocus on building first-party data through CRM integration and direct customer interactions.\r\nAdapt to new targeting methods like cohort-based advertising.\r\nImplement consent management systems to ensure compliance with privacy laws.\r\n138. How will augmented reality (AR) impact Google Ads?\r\nAugmented reality is likely to become a larger part of advertising as AR technology becomes more accessible. Google has already introduced AR capabilities in search results (e.g., users can view 3D models of products in their space). In the future, Google Ads may incorporate AR features to offer more interactive and immersive ad experiences.','2025-03-31 07:11:55','2025-07-13 05:58:06',1,0,1),(68,'Traveling Things','','1- October flat keys\r\n2-powebank\r\n3-headphones\r\n4-mobile and labtop with their chatgers\r\n5- teethpaste and prush\r\n6-medecines and other things of its type\r\n7-wallet\r\n8-rquired clothes\r\n9-Glasses\r\n10- tools kit\n11-others people things\n12- shampoo & Berfume & manadil & Rexona and all hygines \n13- gifts\n14- fruits or sweets \n15- Wallet\n16- coffe','2025-04-02 19:25:53','2026-03-04 23:02:26',1,0,1),(72,'Labtops Ecommerce Business','','Want to create a website abd app with complete ecommerce process where I can sell laptops used  and new mobiles\r\nThese laptops I get from people around me or shops and start market for them on a website , app and a facebook page\r\n\r\nThe dashboatd of the website and app would be the workspace itself to link all your businesses together \r\n\r\n\r\nIntel Processor Generations (Core i3, i5, i7, i9):\r\n\r\n6th Gen (Skylake) – Released in 2015. Introduced DDR4 RAM support and improved battery life.\r\n\r\n7th Gen (Kaby Lake) – 2016. Enhanced 4K video performance and better graphics.\r\n\r\n8th Gen (Kaby Lake R) – 2017. Added more cores, especially for i5 and i7.\r\n\r\n9th Gen (Coffee Lake R) – 2018. Higher clock speeds and improved thermals.\r\n\r\n10th Gen (Ice Lake/Comet Lake) – 2019. Added AI features and better integrated graphics.\r\n\r\n11th Gen (Tiger Lake) – 2020. Introduced Intel Iris Xe graphics and Thunderbolt 4.\r\n\r\n12th Gen (Alder Lake) – 2021. Hybrid design with performance and efficiency cores.\r\n\r\n13th Gen (Raptor Lake) – 2022. Improved performance and battery optimization.\r\n\r\n14th Gen (Meteor Lake) – 2023/2024. Focused on AI tasks and power efficiency.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAMD Ryzen Processor Generations:\r\n\r\n1st Gen (1000 series) – Released in 2017. First Ryzen CPUs with good multi-core performance.\r\n\r\n2nd Gen (2000 series) – 2018. Improved power efficiency and clock speeds.\r\n\r\n3rd Gen (3000 series) – 2019. Built on 7nm architecture, much better performance.\r\n\r\n4th Gen – Skipped on desktops, limited to some laptops.\r\n\r\n5th Gen (5000 series) – 2020. Major performance jump, very competitive with Intel.\r\n\r\n6th Gen (6000 series) – 2022. Integrated RDNA 2 graphics, great for gaming laptops.\r\n\r\n7th Gen (7000 series) – 2023. Supports DDR5 RAM and uses the latest architecture.\r\n\r\nIntel Core i5-8250U -> this means 8th generation because it starts with 8 in 8250u','2025-04-06 06:05:58','2025-08-29 13:33:33',1,0,1),(73,'Transportations','','Always make your flat the center point of your transportations and the start of all of them\r\n\r\nDo not use Ayat Monib transportation except you are forced because it requires too much walking\r\n\r\n1- to travel from Ayat to 1185 go through factories car in tahma and you have to be there at 5AM\r\n\r\n2- to travel from 1185 to Ayat go to mawakf and ride beni suef or wasta or gerza the one that is about to fill up and then take any car going to the entire village (Tahma)\r\n\r\n3- when travelling to souhag make sure to book a go and return tickets at the same time\r\n\r\nAyat  >>> Giza Trains\r\n141  @6:25??\r\n1109@7:21??\r\n143  @9:14\r\n1111@14:06??\r\n147  @15:02\r\n153  @17:40\r\n\r\nGiza >>> Ayat Trains\r\n142 @9:10??\r\n134 @11:15\r\n146 @14:10\r\n1110@16:10??\r\n152  @18:35\r\n196  @ 20:00??','2025-04-07 01:33:49','2025-07-13 05:58:06',1,0,1),(75,'Half Filled Cub','','1- Great gf \r\n2- good jop and good freelance with both of the in 8 hours daily and friday plus saturday vaccancies and remotely with no transportations\r\n3- work space system \r\n4- Flat in October\r\n\r\nAllhumdullah','2025-04-13 16:01:24','2025-07-13 05:58:06',1,0,1),(76,'CV Refrence','','CV Reference\r\n\r\nConcentrate on payment sms google maps services\r\nUse grammarly new feature to rehearse all this file \r\n\r\nContacts\r\nPhone1:01126785910\r\nPhone2:01208050298\r\nphone3:01554532593\r\nEmail1:nessimboula@gmail.com\r\nEmail2:boula.nessim.soliman@gmail.com\r\nEmail3:boula.n.soliman@gmail.com \r\nAddress1: Haddaek ElAhram - Giza\r\nAddress2: Haddaek October - Giza\r\nGithib:https://github.com/boula1997?tab=repositories\r\nLinkedin:https://www.linkedin.com/in/boula-nessim\r\nFacebook: https://www.facebook.com/boula.nessim.7/\r\n\r\nProfessional Summary\r\nSelf-motivated Full-Stack Laravel Developer with over one year of experience collaborating on multiple web-based projects. Passionate and hardworking, with a penchant for developing customized interfaces that prioritize accessibility, reachability, and security. Demonstrates an organized approach to meeting concurrent deadlines and leverages active knowledge of the current technology landscape to promote best practices in web development\r\n\r\nExperience\r\n•	Full Stack Developer at Yousab Tech Company\r\n•	Nov 2023 - Present\r\n•	Collaborate with a team of Full Stack web and mobile developers to create websites and mobile apps for company clients.\r\n•	Utilize technologies such as Laravel, React JS, Angular, and React Native to develop innovative solutions.\r\n•	Full Stack Developer at Marwan Group Company\r\n•	Aug 2022 - Oct 2023\r\n•	Collaborated closely with designers, developers, and project managers to build websites for companies in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia.\r\n•	Developed and maintained web applications using PHP Laravel and Angular, ensuring high-quality deliverables and client satisfaction.\r\n\r\nEducation\r\n•	Bachelor’s Degree in Computer Science\r\n•	Arab Academy for Science, Technology & Maritime Transport (AASTMT)\r\n•	Graduated in 2021\r\n•	Cumulative GPA: 3.3\r\