ery helpful) while copying modules\r\nWe can open project in vscode by drag and drop it to vscode app in taskbar\r\nTo test request and forms in site front part, search for <form and using alt+shift+c copy front views path and start testing them one by one without missing any\r\nWe can use open in editor and copy files paths to perform on them some actions such as git checkout commit -m – path once \r\ngit checkout 1817e31 -- app/Http/Controllers/admin/OrderController.php\r\ngit checkout 1817e31 -- database/migrations/2022_02_13_085549_create_orders_table.php\r\ngit checkout 1817e31 -- database/migrations/2022_02_13_085602_create_order_details_table.php\r\ngit checkout 1817e31 -- resources/views/admin/orders/index.blade.php\r\ngit checkout 1817e31 -- resources/views/admin/layouts/aside.blade.php\r\ngit checkout 1817e31 -- routes/admin.php\r\ngit checkout 1817e31 -- resources/lang/en/general.php\r\ngit checkout 1817e31 -- resources/lang/ar/general.php\r\nwe can do magic using mysql SELECT DISTINCT  COLUMN_NAME,DATA_TYPE  from INFORMATION_SCHEMA. COLUMNS where table_schema = \'marwan_group\' order by DATA_TYPE; especially regarding translations validations and we can translate 80% of site using it by using all inputs in atrributes:en and atrributes:ar and attributes also using them in lang/general.php \r\nIt is possible to use ctrl+d & ctrl+k for doing code on not similar selected sentences or words to write edits once at the same time\r\nWe can get all the columns in tables in one table using SQL command SELECT DISTINCT  TABLE_NAME,COLUMN_NAME,DATA_TYPE  from INFORMATION_SCHEMA. COLUMNS where table_schema = \'marwan_group\' and COLUMN_NAME NOT IN (\"id\",\"locale\",\"updated_at\",\"created_at\",\"status\") order by TABLE_NAME;\r\n\r\nWe can use this function to check if a variable is object is_object($var)\r\n-When creatin a fullstack site (Angular or bootstrap Laravel) use a ready one and edit it to be like the one you want to create  \r\nAlways think about editing a module or adding a module that there is a string or path or track that I can detect using a common keyword at all the module files and I have to think about this keyword carefully to save effort and time \r\nThe best way to reach file path is searching for url end word ex: https://yousab-tech.com/dashboard/pages\r\nSearch for pages to reach files you will edit\r\nCreate a new module by changing current module and keep both of them for more info see methodologies down and when changing file names use pageup and pagedown to make it easier\r\nIt is really important to use Search inside search results methodology at all your coding time\r\nDisable ck editor while testing website to easily use fake filler in it using ctrl+shift+f\r\nuse ctrl+shift+e //to take o\r\nAlways us alt+d when using browse to get file you want fast and easily\r\n\r\nAdd folders that contain uploaded images and documents (uploads) to git ignore to make it easy to sync between projects in local and server and also be able to edit database and sync them without affecting files\r\n\r\nAlways create a folder to contain all non apps and make desktop clean\r\n\r\nAlways put these words (	d) in exclude of vscode search and it is recommended to put them in text file on desktop to easily reach them \r\nSet git bash as default profile in vscode \r\n\r\nIt is very important to set a key besides tab and shift + tab to work as enter in order to navigate pages easily without using mouse\r\nAlways use seeders in filling websites data (without images) and take image name from images folder after uploading them from dashboard instead of database\r\nAlways use ssh as your server terminal \r\nWhen using tab button in terminal it gives us all the option to choose from for example when writin path it gives me folders or files inside the last written path \r\nAlways use dark mode for everything on your computer\r\nAlways test files system in your dashboard by removing all files from public and database and check if default image replace them\r\nAlways use multi images in pages module and give a condition with number of images needed for pages that need more than one image to not show if user uploaded less than two\r\nChange your dashboard to tomato php \r\nIf there is a dropdown input, you can add modal to add new without having to go back and fill data from the module home on dashboard\r\nWhen get new module from other repo take only the files that contains only module data and do not take files that contain all modules data such as routes and lang files\r\nWhen testing a website responsiveness, test it from your mobile phone\r\nSoftware is all about making easy easier\r\nwhen git pull and get merge warning to avoid merge you can stash your work and pull then stash pop your work again\r\n\r\nif navbar is not toggling add js code to toggle it manually and remove id ex: id=\"navbarCollapse\" to prevent bootstrap js code\r\n\r\nAlways use cmd as your default terminal\r\nYou must put inspect on left side to make it easy for you to read errors\r\nAlways set wordWrap in vscode to on\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(11,'Try or learn\r\nmin and max html attributes for date input\r\nhasMany and hasOne and belongsToMany\r\nrequest->merge\r\nattach and detach methods\r\nhttps://www.amitmerchant.com/attach-detach-sync-laravel/\r\ndatetime to get tomorrow date\r\nOTP authentication\r\nGuards laravel\r\nhttps://techvblogs.com/blog/multiple-authentication-guards-laravel-9\r\nAuto scroll in chat\r\nLoading and 404 page\r\nTraits in laravel\r\nhttps://www.positronx.io/laravel-traits-example/\r\nCreate a crud project using node js and mongodb\r\nhttps://blog.appsignal.com/2022/08/17/build-a-crud-app-with-nodejs-and-mongodb.html\r\nrepositories in php and laravel\r\nhttps://larainfo.com/blogs/laravel-9-repository-design-pattern-crud-example\r\nlaravel unit test\r\nhttps://laravel.com/docs/10.x/http-tests\r\nthrough one through many\r\nwith in laravel eloquent\r\nfindMany($idsArray)\r\nLaravel email verification\r\nhttps://www.itsolutionstuff.com/post/laravel-custom-email-verification-system-exampleexample.html\r\nroute (group,prefix,middleware,namespace)\r\nforelse\r\nmorph\r\nstorage\r\nEloquent Relationship\r\nhas & orhas\r\norwhere\r\nwhereRelation\r\ndoesntHave\r\nwhereDoesntHave\r\nwithCount\r\nintended in routing\r\nCypress https://www.cypress.io/ //for testing websites\r\nLodash\r\nhttps://lodash.com/docs/4.17.15 \r\ntoastify package\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(12,'Solid Principles\r\nSingle Responsibility\r\nOpen Closed\r\nLiskov Substitution\r\nInterface Segregation\r\nDependency Inversion\r\nNote: DO NOT initiate and run functions at same file\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(13,'Very boring work tasks\r\nChecking translationa:solved\r\nTesting website:solved\r\nEdit migrations:solved\r\nCopying modules and features from another repo:solved\r\nChanging dashboard from code style to different code style:solved\r\nDealing with database easily and simply in terminal:solved \r\nMost other boring tasks are solved by keyboard shortcuts, extensions and notes.\r\nNavigation in vscode:solved by Remember Open Files extension\r\nCopying module lang from another project:Solved by lang methodology down\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(14,'Very IMPORTANT way to test and fix all translations in web app \r\nYou could install a package like: https://github.com/barryvdh/laravel-translation-manager  \r\nThis will expose a UI and some artisan commands which will allow you to check for untranslated strings per namespace/language and edit them.\r\nThis package does however require an additional table which will hold the translation.\r\nYou can use the artisan commands:\r\nphp artisan translations:import\r\nTo import translations from you translation files into the db table\r\nphp artisan translations:find\r\nTo scan through your blade files and find untranslated strings\r\nphp artisan translations:export\r\nTo export changes made in the package UI and write back to the translation files, after which you can simply commit your changes.\r\nphp artisan translations:reset \r\nTo clear translations and cache\r\nNote we have to run both php artisan translations:import and php artisan translations:find to be able to detect null translations values and in sequence. Because import get all translations in lang while find get all translations in views and by running both they are merged and translations with null value appear.\r\nNote: This way does not cover validations so for validation do the following \r\nNote: use select * from ltm_translations where value IS NULL; sql command to get translations with no value\r\n1-get all the inputs names using mysql SELECT DISTINCT  COLUMN_NAME,DATA_TYPE  from INFORMATION_SCHEMA. COLUMNS where table_schema = \'marwan_group\' order by DATA_TYPE;\r\n2- copy these name and translate the them in lang files\r\n3-use all of them in attributes and also all of them in attributes:en and also all of them in attributes:ar\r\nFor English put the as they are with removing _id fro fields that have it\r\nFor Arabic, translate all of them once using google translate extension alt+shift+t. After that add ال to them and translate wrong value translations.\r\n\r\nNote: to make it easy for you work only on new added modules because old are already translated and tested\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(15,'Final web app Testing methodology\r\n1- Test all translations locally using the translations package methodology\r\n2-get all routes and filter them to the only used routes.\r\n3-test on server version (YOU MUST TAKE PUBLIC FOLDER BACKUP AND DATA OF DATABASE BACKUP BEFORE TESTING)\r\n4-Test validations, validations translations with empty fields, validations translations with filled fields (using fake filler)and create only by opening all create routes \r\n5- Test other site cruds(edit,show,delete) by opening all index routes and use ctrl+click to open other them for each module \r\n6-test all get apis on browser and compare the to database in terminal and post apis on postman\r\n7-Delete unused modules using ctrl+shift+f to reach all module files\r\n8-remove folder where you save files from git ignore to test file system delete\r\n9-use files extensions especially Open Matching Files extension\r\n10-use php artisan route:list --columns=uri,method --sort=method //show specific column to easily get routes names\r\n11-to give value for edit and show routes ex:/{slider} duplicate create route and change create with 1 and same for /{slider}/edit to be /1/edit\r\n\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(16,'Last create new module methodology\r\n\r\nNote: To make best use of this great methodology, you have to concentrate on naming all the module attributes such as variables in blades and anything else.\r\n\r\nWe need to use crate and edit module both together when the new module does not have all the requirements and it is better to first create all the missing modules and then edit them \r\nCreate New module\r\n1- Replace old module keyword with new module keyword (cap with cap and small with small)\r\nNote : Result will be\r\n\r\n.files with old module name\r\n.files with content related to old module\r\n.files that are not related to old module\r\nNote:module name in arabic will be the same so replace it too with new module arabic name (twice singular and plural)\r\n2- stage files with old module name and restore files that are unrelated to old module and keep file that has content for the old module \r\n\r\nNote: use search in files list in this step\r\n\r\n3-Add content to the new module for files that has content about the old module \r\n4-open staged (select them and right click and choose open file) files and rename them to new module name\r\n5- restore deleted files produced by prev process to keep old module and then use Edit existing module Attributes to have all the new module requirments\r\n\r\n\r\nEdit existing module Attributes\r\n1- Replace  module keyword with boulasflag (without enabling case sensitive Aa)\r\nNote : Result will be\r\n.files with  module name\r\n.files with content related to module\r\n.files that are not related to old module\r\n\r\n\r\n2- stage files with module name and \r\nfile that has content for the module and restore files that are unrelated to module\r\n\r\n3- open all changed files then restore all changed files\r\n\r\n4-replace all boulasflag with module keyword (reverse step 1) to to reset changes in files outside git\r\n\r\n5- add or remove attributes using search in opened files only\r\nNote: If the attribute is weird do not replace all and replace it or add it file by file using ctrl+f not ctrl+shift+f\r\n\r\nCreate new module from a pull request\r\n1-git pull \r\n2- unstage them to get rid of merge\r\n3-stage needed files only\r\n4-restore other files\r\n5- edit modified files M and leave untracked files U\r\n6- when editing modified files copy old version code and copy the part from the new version and merge them to only add this new  part to old version\r\n\r\nBig Note: We can add the old module data when comparing by duplicate the result and move it using alt+arrow Down and then use arrow in comparison to get the old value\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(17,'Testing using all crud routes\r\n1-take backup for data and uploads folder\r\n1-Get all routes using php artisan route list\r\n2-Customize them to get only used module crud routes\r\n3-change the {id} or {model} with 1\r\n4-export data only for database and change abstractly the first record id of each table to be 1\r\n5-Migrate fresh and import the modified data and enjoy testing\r\n6- test design then translations then validations then technicality (crud)\r\n7- test them separately i.e: indexes then deletes creates then edits then shows using Open Matching Files extension\r\n8- return backup\r\n9-when debugging and need pacific file use url and search in routes only methodologies\r\n10- first take notes about errors and then fix them once\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(18,'Very Very Very IMPORTANT TO APPLY IN CODING\r\nWhen we use compare methodology, we can compare between files by unstage them and open files in changes and start get the merged needed one by copy and paste or clicking the arrow -> for each.\r\nAlso use git stash and git stash pop to test the copied feature\r\n\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(19,'very important five ways to apply comparison methodology among files\r\n1-git checkout origin/main . helps me compare and edit files after they are changed. \r\n2-git reset commit –soft helps me compare and edit files in their current version.\r\n3- Just change the file\'s content. And is mostly used when the code we need to use is in a different path of the receiver or has a different name.\r\n4- git revert helps me to compare but I have to commit changes first.\r\n5- git pull origin main helps to compare but it must pull all the files on repo.\r\nNote: \r\n1-Take about click to revert change option while editing on files after using one of these files\r\n2-The most important way is git reset commit –soft because it helps me to edit the current version from the pulled version and also enables me to test pulled modules easily while comparing. So, it must always be used. And I have to pull on other projects instances using git reset commit –hard and push using -f.\r\n3-We can get rid of untracked U and added files A by using git stash or we can un stage all changes and stage untracked only using git add -i and follow steps.\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(20,'Class+$loop->index and attribute index={{$loop->index}} Methodology (Jquery)\r\nUsage: Access element using jquery\r\nTo access an element add to the event element attribute index=”{{$loop->index}}”\r\nAnd add to the class of element the will be affected by this event class=”{{$loop->index}}” to avoid using nex parent and children too mcuch\r\n\r\nReturn this in laravel refrence.docx for an example using code\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(21,'Extremely important new coding methodology \r\n1- Use the Remember Open Files extension to open all module files you are creating or editing and other static files that are always used for all modules ex:routes.\r\nNote: do not open files (using the extension) that can be reached from other files ex: model, views and request can be reached from extension.\r\n2- when you need to work on another module, just open a json file used by extension to store files paths and change those paths to the new module files paths.\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(22,'Extremely important new coding methodology to create new module \r\nFirst way\r\n1-choose a similar module \r\n2-open its files using Remember Open Files extension\r\n3- edit it to has totally all requirements of the new module \r\n4- when the new module is ready, change the  names (including classes names)inside module files and change files names \r\n5- compare and keep both modules\r\n6-migrate and run laratrust seeder\r\n7- push both modules\r\nNote: this great way can be used for backend and frontend tasks\r\nNote: when changing old module name to new module name \r\nfirst, replace small words\r\nsecond, replace capital letter\r\nDeal with them as singular only and if there are miss spelled plural change them abstractly at the end\r\nex of miss spelled plural: company = companys\r\n\r\nSecond way (currently used)\r\n1-choose a similar module\r\n2-use abstract search to search for module keyword for example module products search for product\r\n3-customize search results to include module files only\r\n4-use abstract replace to change product with new module name say product with course  and Product with Course\r\n5-Change file names \r\n6-restore old modules files in source control\r\n7-migrate new module and seed laratrust seeders \r\nNote: use ctrl+pageUp and ctrl+pageDown while changing files names\r\nuse search only changes files\r\nNote: while replacing module name use only singular word ex:company and take care about miss spelled plural ex:company companys redo replacement with the correct plural companies\r\nNote: use git add -i to add only untracked and level modified and deleted files make it easy to you to focus on them\r\nMost professional work methodology\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(23,'New effective last Coding methodology to get module from another project (Currently used)\r\n1-get all the files you want paths using alt shift us and MMCRRRVASL and search for module keyword to easily reach module files\r\n2-get code snippets needed such as routes\r\n3-git checkout them using git and copy code snippet\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(24,'New effective last Coding methodology to copy module lang content(Currently used)\r\n1-search for module keyword \r\n2-open in editor \r\n3- search for keyword in editor using ctrl+f2 and copy all lines with this keyword\r\n4- select all and paste them to get rid of the unrelated words \r\n5- customize them and copy them to lang files \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(25,'Multiple copy methodology\r\nUsage :\r\nVery useful in creating seeders, translations and other similar modules.\r\nDescription:determine a block of statements and work on them once.\r\nExtensions needed \r\nShift+alt+i\r\nCtrl+f2,Ctrl+D,ctrl+c,ctrl+v\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(26,'Using templates methodology\r\nTemplate css and assets files must be put in folder named template and do not edit then instead create file custom.css \r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(27,'Search inside search results or open all search results files methodology (IMPORTANT Currently used)\r\nModually\r\n1-search for a keyword that can open all the module files (usually module name)\r\n2-change keyword to flag\r\n3- open changed files\r\n4- restore changed files\r\n5-search again for the word you work on in opened files by enabling the book icon\r\nNote: helps a lot when adding or removing an element or some elements from a module (edit module not create new one)\r\n\r\nGenerally\r\n1-search for word \r\n2- replace word with flag \r\n3-open changed files\r\n4-restore changed files\r\n5- search for word you want in opened files by clicking opened book icon in search side menu\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(28,'Copy module by keyword & path methodology\r\n1-search for required module keyword in project that has the module you want to copy \r\n2- Make sure that you get the right path or track by choosing a keyword that is common in all the module files\r\n3- copy these module files paths \r\n4- git checkout to all of them in your project  \r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(29,'Navigate and db ref methodology\r\nnavigate using routes file \r\nget db info using db ref file \r\nNote:routes file are created using routes from command route list with adding domain to them \r\nand dbref file are created with show columns command in mysql terminal and cousomize them by adding desc before each table and ; at the end and run them in mysql terminal\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(30,'Navigate using flag methodology\r\ncopy a sentence from one of two code blocks and use it in second one as a flag\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(31,'fold methodology\r\ncopy a sentence where you want the fold to be and fold all using ctrl+k+0 and search for sentence\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(32,'test files methodology\r\nremove public from gitignore and start test adding and removing files from source control section in vscode\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(33,'pin to clipboard methodology\r\nPin local and demo website links (domains) to clipboard to reach them while testing easily\r\nroutes as a word to help reach a specific file or view\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(34,'New test methodology\r\n1-take post routes which we get from php artisan route:list –columns=method,uri,action –sort=method as reference while testing\r\n2-reach files by url in browser\r\n3-move between modules using alt+arrow right and alt +arrow left in browser\r\n4-always use open in editor option in search while testing\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(35,'New test methodology\r\n1-Create new module files\r\n2-replace content with the similar module\r\n3-git add \r\n4-compare using arrows to replace the old module name\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(36,'End to top copy methodology\r\nWhen copying a feature from another module take it from end to top to appear in clipboard ordered and take it all once from each file in module\r\nUse OpenMatching File to help in this\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(37,'open all module files methodology (very important)\r\n1-do abstract search for module keyword\r\n2-open in editor\r\n3-copy only paths and paste them to get rid of content\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(38,'Solve migration not found problem\r\n$ php artisan migrate:rollback --path=database/migrations/2022_12_11_090145_create_category_translations_table.php\r\nMigration not found: 2023_01_23_130256_create_gallery_translations_table\r\nMigration not found: 2023_01_23_125628_create_galleries_table\r\nwhen got this error I have to run php artisan migrate:rollback\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(39,'Strange foreign key errors while migration\r\nCheck in table operations that storage engine is similar\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(40,'Using keyboard only in vscode\r\n1-use ctrl+e to select files you need to copy code from when you are creating new module\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(41,'html important property\r\ndiv>h1>p give us code with this tags\r\nwith classes also div.row>div.col-md-3\r\ninput:number\r\ninput:password\r\na:link\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(42,'Multiple words capitalize method\r\n1-choose words you want to capitalize using ctrl+D and ctrl+k to skip words that should not be capitalized\r\n2-select only the first letter of these words\r\n3-ctrl+shift+p and choose uppercase \r\nnote:there is also lowercase option\r\n\r\nctrl+shift+e magic\r\nDesc: extension to take a screenshot of a full web page\r\nUsage: comparing between two websites when trying to create one from the other.\r\nAlso used to detect design bugs \r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(43,'Sync files and database methodology\r\n1-add uploads folder to git ignore\r\n2- sync between files between server and local\r\n3- migrate fresh local and import database of server \r\n4- edit on database in local and export it to server \r\n5- now we have synced database and synced files with no effort\r\nctrl+shift+e magic\r\nDesc: extension to take a screenshot of a full web page\r\nUsage: comparing between two websites when trying to create one from the other.\r\nAlso used to detect design bugs \r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(44,'How do you change the capitalization of filenames in Git?\r\n1-git config --global core.ignorecase false\r\n2- git mv resources/views/admin/blogs/Index.blade.php resources/views/admin/blogs/index.blade.php – force \r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(45,'How to get design mentor or reference for your frontend work\r\n1-download free templates from themeforest and free css websites and others as a reference for all your website components\r\n2- Try to create the content and make it similar instead of copying it (copy it if time is not enough to create)\r\n3- take different components from different free templates\r\n4-create a notebook and save the part you chose from each website foreach component\r\nex:\r\nabout -> https://www.free-css.com/free-css-templates/page294/jobentry\r\nsliders -> https://www.free-css.com/free-css-templates/page294/jobentry\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(46,'Poly search methodology\r\nIt is used when we want to search for some word and need to save the pace where we are going copy it\r\n1-use normal search to find the keyword of part where you are working\r\n2-use abstract search to find the keyword of section where you are going to copy from \r\nNote: this can be used if the two sections(section where i will copy from and section where i will copy to) are in the same page or even in different pages \r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(47,'How to enable dark mode for everything in your chrome browser\r\n1-got to chrome://flags/\r\n2- search for darkmode\r\n3- enable Enabled with simple HSL-based inversion\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(48,'Catch errors methodology\r\n1-add try and catch to functions in controller\r\n2- use dd($e->getMessage()) to show the error\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(49,'Change ltr template to rtl methodology\r\n1-change template style.css to style_ar.css as follow\r\n right to boulasflag and left to right then change boulasflag to left\r\n2- crate a condition to separate between two files (style and style_ar) and also add bootstrap and bootstrap.rel according to lang \r\nex:\r\n @if (app()->getLocale()==\'en\')\r\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"{{asset(\'bootstrap-5.3.1-dist\\css\\bootstrap.min.css\')}}\"\r\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"{{ asset(\'dist/css/adminlte.min.css\') }}\">\r\n    @else\r\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"{{asset(\'bootstrap-5.3.1-dist\\css\\bootstrap.rtl.min.css\')}}\">\r\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"{{ asset(\'dist/css/adminlte.min_ar.css\') }}\">\r\n    @endif\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(50,'Do it once methodology\r\nUsage: used when we are going to add something like old() to all inputs in a blase\r\nProcess: do ctrl+d to name=” and do ctrl+f2 to select all of them then stand at first of name=” and and write {{old(‘’)}} then go with cursor to after name=” and do ctrl+d and ctrl+f2 to select all and then move cursor to ‘’ in old and paste\r\nNote (very new and important): if word you are copying to ,, consist of two or more equal parts use ctrl+shift+arrowright to copy them all once   \r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(51,'Do it once methodology\r\nUsage: if you want to return some edits and keep others in same file or different files\r\nprocess: do git reset commit –soft using very old commit and then search for module files in git tree and edit them to choose what to keep and what to return using center arrows ->\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(52,'Open multi modules methodology\r\nUsage:Open more than one module together or when you are working on a task that requires you to open two modules that are in relation\r\nprocess: using Edit existing module Attributes and open all modules you want\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(53,'Getting old edits methodology\r\n1- do git log –all and copy all commits in new file in vscode\r\n2-search in this file for edits keyword to get its commit\r\n3- git checkout commit . for theses commits from old to new\r\n4- choose required files only and discard files mix or collect many modules together to add them manually\r\n5- open changed files\r\n6-start to handle what was not added to complete task\r\n\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(54,'How to make your website reusable and easy to edit on it\r\n1- create seeders for all site data\r\n2- mian pages like breadcrumb must have image input in setting\r\n3- add all translation in one file for each lang for example ar/general.php and en/general.php and use the translations package to get what need to be translated\r\n4- name all module files with the module name to easily open them once and edit on module quickly and also othe code snippet for the module should have its name\r\n5- use Common module files Methodology\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(55,'Laravel and angular (php and js) debug methodology\r\nAngular and js  alert()\r\nLaravel and php return\r\nlaravel dd()\r\nAll: try{}catch(){} with ( alert() for js and angular, dd for laravel or return for php\r\nIt is really effective to use try and catch with this great debug methods)\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(56,'Open all module methodology\r\nWhen working on a module it is very effective to open all its files that contain the module name to make it easy for you to edit on it\r\n\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(57,'create new pages in front methodology\r\nAfter creating home page start with adding all other pages routes in header blade and then start creating them through checking errors and solve them\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(58,'Magical multi copy methodology\r\nSelect parts of many lines to copy them to other parts of these lines or even other lines using ctrl +shift + arrow right or arrow left depending on copy word by word not letter by letter. So, we can copy unequal parts that have the same count of words. It is really magic.\r\nHowever with the help of Quick and Simple Text Selection vscode extension we can now do that for tgese lines that have different number of parts\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(59,'Translation magic methodology\r\n1-use translations package\r\n2- get all what need to be translated\r\n3- copy and customize them in vscode to be all in one file and has same first word such as words.something or general.something\r\n4- copy words and translate them in english and arabic using multi copy methodology\r\n6- show all website variables using sql command and translate them in arabic and english and copy them to validations lang\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(60,'Unique component methodology\r\nwhen creating the laravel project components, if we have a section such as services and it is different in design in home and services page do not create two service components. Just create one component and handle differences using conditions using conditions on route if(request()->routeIs()).\r\n\r\nAlso if you have about component that has to have a limit text and button that leads to creating only one about component and handle differences using conditions on route if(request()->routeIs()).\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(61,'Route first methodology\r\nstart adding any section or page or even module by adding its route and then other things\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(62,'Create module once and use many\r\nUsage: its used when we have many projects that share similar dashboard and we wan to add new module for example products to all of them\r\nprocess:\r\n1-create the new module in one of them and commit it in one commit and push\r\n2- Nav to the second project and link with the old project repo and get the commit and do the checkout commit .\r\n3- choose only from git tree files that relates to the newly added module\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(63,'Module name files methodology\r\nWhen getting old module from old git commits, return only files with the module name and add its content in files that does not have the module name and these files are \r\nroutes: web.php admin.php api.php\r\nblades: dashboard.php\r\npermissions: PermissionTableSeeder.php\r\nlang files: general.php validation.php\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(64,'Very Big Note on all methodologies\r\nWhen adding a new module or get old module using git, just work on the file that gas the module name and other files that are likely routes and sidebar and permissionSeeder add them manually. And always care about giving the module name in its files and content as much as you can.\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(65,'Include and exclude\r\nlaravel\r\ninclude: .php,.css\r\nexclude:storage,vendor\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(66,'Common module files Methodology\r\nFiles that contain data for all modules and have add modules to it manually to make it easy to get or create the new module without making a lot of comparisons \r\nbrief: prscl\r\n1-routes\r\n2-sidebar\r\n3-cards counts\r\n4-permissions seeder\r\n5-lang\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(67,'Unique module name files methodology (The most important)\r\nModule unique files must have the module name to make it easy to create similar modules using other methodologies\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(68,'Last create new module methodology {Most Important}\r\nGet the new unique module files (files that have the module name) from the existing module and then add its content to files that have all other modules content as follows.\r\n\r\nFiles that contain data for all modules, add new module content to it manually to make it easy to get or create the new module without making a lot of comparisons \r\nbrief: prscl hh\r\n1-routes\r\n2-sidebar\r\n3-cards counts\r\n4-permissions seeder\r\n5-lang\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(69,'Create and edit methodology (fix create and get edit for free)\r\nYou can edit on create.blade.php and then copy all create content and paste it in edit.blade.php and then select all old and using multi edit to copy input name in old and paste it as $module->name\r\n\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(70,'Project dividing\r\ncreate components to every entity in website\r\n\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(71,'Create all project modules once methodology\r\n1-Create all modules unique files (files that have the module name) using above methodologies\r\n2-Create other file using prscl h from methodologies above\r\n3-start adding inputs to modules migrations\r\n4- add these inputs to other modules files using (MMCCRRSV) and database terminal as a reference and the help of above methodologies (open all migrations once and start move through them and add inputs to them)\r\n5- copy module inputs from terminal and paste them to stick note \r\n6- open the module files manually using ctrl+e and (MMCCRRSV) and and move through them in order from start to end using ctrl+pageDown and start working \r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(72,'Magic edit many sentences once  methodology\r\nSelection + alt+shift+i + ctrl+d\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(73,'Open module files methodology (overrides on all similar above methodologies)\r\n1-ctrl+shift+f to find all files with module keyword\r\n2-open them manually from search results\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(74,'Moving through files methodology\r\nNote: make working on adding inputs to module very easy\r\n1-move through module files you are working on using ctrl+pageUp and ctrl+pageDown\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(75,'Open module files methodology (applicable and must be in use)\r\n1-ctrl+shift+f\r\n2-select files from search side and drag them to tabs bar (Important do not forget)\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(76,'Dashboard Files\r\n#Pure module files\r\nMMCCRRSV\r\nMigration Model \r\nController api Controller admin\r\nRequest Resource\r\nSeeder View\r\n\r\n#Modules container files\r\nPRSCLH\r\nPermission Route Sidebar Count Lang Helper\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(77,'Open related task files methodology (Important)\r\nWhen working on any task open the files related to the task by searching for the keyword and start dragging the files from the search results and after that start searching on inputs names in these files only using search only on Open Editor option marked as book in vscode \r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(78,'Using remote terminal locally methodology\r\n1-	Open terminal\r\n2-	ssh cpanelusername@IPaddress -p2222\r\n3-	choose yes\r\n4-	cPanel password\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(79,'Mult Desktop Methodology\r\n1-	press windows+tab and create new desktop \r\n2-	Drag tabs that are important and have to be safe to desktop (Remote terminal + sticky notes)\r\n \r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(80,'.env email example\r\nMAIL_MAILER=smtp\r\nMAIL_HOST=mail.demoyoursite.net\r\nMAIL_PORT=465\r\nMAIL_USERNAME=contact@demoyoursite.net\r\nMAIL_PASSWORD=u@159753@\r\nMAIL_ENCRYPTION=ssl\r\nMAIL_FROM_ADDRESS=contact@demoyoursite.net\r\nMAIL_FROM_NAME=\"${APP_NAME}\"\r\nQUEUE_DRIVER=database\r\n\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(81,'Open Matching KeyWord files methodology (Most Important to edit or create modules)\r\nUsage: used when we want to open all files that contain some word for examble user using vscode  extension Open Matching Files \r\n1-	Alt+f and search for *user*.php and users/*.blade.php to open all user module files\r\n2-	Press enter\r\n3-	Work on file in sequence using ctrl+pageUp and ctrl+pageDown and alt+1 to start from first file\r\nNote: to make the best out of this methodology, you have to customize search setting to exclude unneeded files such as storage and vendor and also name module files with modle name and show file list usin ctrl + shift + E to make it easy for you to read files names while moving through them\r\n4-	If there are refrence use it by searching on opened files and start copy and paste the refrence content in each file (very effective to use)\r\n5-	Note: Alt+f and search for */*api*/* to open all api files and all files inside any folder has api keyword\r\n\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(82,'General Coding Methodolgy (Important)\r\n1-	Project must be divided into mdoules\r\n2-	Each module should have the mdoule keyword\r\n3-	Use Open Matching KeyWord files methodology\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(83,'How to get Unauthenticated message in tymon auth api\r\nIf you send the Accept header as application/json this will cause the Exception Handler to return JSON when handling the Unauthorized Exception\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(84,'Restore multibe deleted files methodology\r\nWe can select all deleted files from git workspace and restore them once to avoid the deleted restore message to appear many times\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(85,'Open local websites on mobile and labtop at the same time to to responsivity matters \r\nOn the mobile device, open a web browser and enter the IP address of the computer running the web server, followed by the port number if necessary. For example, if the IP address is 192.168. 1.100 and the web server is listening on port 8000, you would enter “http://192.168.1.100:8000” in the browser\'s address bar.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(86,'Open local websites on mobile and labtop at the same time to to responsivity matters methodology\r\nOn the mobile device, open a web browser and enter the IP address of the computer running the web server, followed by the port number if necessary. For example, if the IP address is 192.168. 1.100 and the web server is listening on port 8000, you would enter “http://192.168.1.100:8000” in the browser\'s address bar.\r\nNote: We can also open debugger on pc and use mopile to show debug on pc\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(87,'Find element data of elements on browser and search for them easily in project code methodology\r\nWe can fin data of all elements of website using the extension show html and we can know tag, class and id and that also help us to search for element in project code files\r\nhttps://stackoverflow.com/questions/37256331/is-it-possible-to-open-developer-tools-console-in-chrome-on-android-phone\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(88,'Increase work productivity methodology(The most important)\r\n\r\nUsage: organize and accelerate work plus increase productivity\r\n1- divide all work day into tasks using pen and paper \r\n2- use Todo Tree vscode extension\r\n3- make someone tell you the tasks one by one while you are adding them using tree todo extension and writing who will do what for each task \r\n4- to add tasks quickly copy <Todo (boula)> and change it accordingly to avoid using alt+shift+f\r\n5- if you found any additional while working add them directly\r\n6- Ask your team to add tasks directly once they found them while testing or even while coding \r\n7- after adding all tasks search for all of them using ctrl+shift+f and write easy in tasks that will not take much time to finish them first after that do this process again and again until finishing all of them\r\n\r\nNote: This methodology must be always used and if extension became unavailable use similar tools especially those which will link task with start code and file\r\n\r\nNote: writing tasks inside code is severely important to reach them easily and update them with team using git and also to use git advantages with tasks like return to deleted tasks when needed\r\n\r\nNote: when meeting clients you must take notes using pen and paper to be able to apply this methodology\r\n\r\nNote: if todo tree vscode extension was not available, find tasks using ctrl + shift + f  to search for them and lust them in search results\r\n\r\nPerform them according to difficulty\r\n\r\nNote: use with this methodology the multiple project methodology\r\n\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(89,'Multiple project methodology\r\nUsage: working on many project at the same time \r\n1- open three desktop tabs and for each tab open a project and run it on chrome \r\n3-	using increase working productivity methodology start working on them together \r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(90,'Start working day methodology\r\nUsage Save time by starting the working day with opening a desktop for each project I will work on and add the following to it \r\n1-	vscode project\r\n2-	remote terminal with cd project\r\n3-	serve website on google\r\n4-	terminal database optional\r\n5-	postman optional\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(91,'General automatic code methodology using terminal and git commands (Make all methodologies easy and automatic) (Most Important I swear)\r\n1-	Use Git ls-files to get all the project files and you can copy needed files by selecting a keyword and use ctrl + f2 to choose all paths that contain this word and we also can filter needed extensions using ctrl + f2\r\n2-	Do what ever processesypu want on these files using terminal command \r\ncode –r app/helpers/helper.php //opens file and create it if not found\r\nren app\\Http\\Controllers\\Admin\\CopyController.php  PasteController.php //rename file\r\ndel – f app\\Http\\Controllers\\Admin\\CopyController.php //delete file\r\nuse Regex search .* to search for multible words and cliuck alt + enter to add cursor for all search words\r\n(product)|(order)|(store)  \r\n\r\nUsages:\r\nClear unused modules\r\nClear unused files (images, videos, pdfs ..etc)\r\nCreate new module\r\nOpen module files\r\nRename module files\r\nCopy module from other project using git\r\nDo the prscl h easily using\r\ncode –r app/helpers/helper.php\r\ncode –r database/seeders/PermissionTableSeeder.php\r\ncode –r resources/lang/ar/general.php\r\ncode –r resources/lang/en/general.php\r\ncode –r resources/views/dashboard.blade.php\r\ncode –r resources/views/admin/components/dashboard.blade.php\r\ncode –r routes/admin.php\r\ncode –r routes/api.php\r\ncode –r routes/web.php\r\n\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(92,'Automaticly create a new module (Complete Guide)\r\n1-	Get the module files using git ls-files\r\n2-	Do as follow rename old module files to new module name and restore old module deleted files \r\nUsing git command {git checkout commit -- path} or {git checkout origin/main -- path}\r\nexample \r\ngit checkout origin/main -- app/Http/Controllers/ServiceController.php\r\ngit checkout origin/main -- app/Http/Controllers/ServiceRequestController.php\r\ngit checkout origin/main -- app/Http/Controllers/Admin/ServiceController.php\r\ngit checkout origin/main -- app/Http/Controllers/Admin/ServiceRequestController.php\r\ngit checkout origin/main -- app/Http/Controllers/API/ServiceController.php\r\ngit checkout origin/main -- app/Http/Requests/ServiceRequestRequest.php\r\ngit checkout origin/main -- app/Http/Requests/API/ServiceRequestRequest.php\r\ngit checkout origin/main -- app/Http/Requests/Dashboard/ServiceRequest.php\r\nor\r\ngit checkout 358922e46c822d513b9959b3a02fc9d64f63ebdc -- app/Http/Controllers/ServiceController.php\r\ngit checkout 358922e46c822d513b9959b3a02fc9d64f63ebdc -- app/Http/Controllers/ServiceRequestController.php\r\ngit checkout 358922e46c822d513b9959b3a02fc9d64f63ebdc -- app/Http/Controllers/Admin/ServiceController.php\r\ngit checkout 358922e46c822d513b9959b3a02fc9d64f63ebdc -- app/Http/Controllers/Admin/ServiceRequestController.php\r\ngit checkout 358922e46c822d513b9959b3a02fc9d64f63ebdc -- app/Http/Controllers/API/ServiceController.php\r\ngit checkout 358922e46c822d513b9959b3a02fc9d64f63ebdc -- app/Http/Requests/ServiceRequestRequest.php\r\ngit checkout 358922e46c822d513b9959b3a02fc9d64f63ebdc -- app/Http/Requests/API/ServiceRequestRequest.php3-Opening shared module files using code –r path{Used for sharded modules files}\r\nLaravel module shared files example \r\ncode –r app/helpers/helper.php\r\ncode –r database/seeders/PermissionTableSeeder.php\r\ncode –r resources/lang/ar/gener\r\n4-add missing module code for each file\r\n6-	change module inputs according to new module requirments \r\nNote: To change input easily you have to have an input component that contain all inputs annd take attributes that \r\ndetermine how the input should be. That will save effort and time\r\n7-use Regex search .* to search for multible words and cliuck alt + enter to add cursor for all search words\r\n(product)|(order)|(store)  \r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(93,'Magic sticks \r\nReady to do magic?\r\ngit ls-files\r\nRegex search .*\r\n(product)|(order)|(store)  \r\nAlt + enter \r\ndel - f path \r\ncode -r path \r\nren path word\r\nSELECT DISTINCT  TABLE_NAME,COLUMN_NAME,DATA_TYPE  from INFORMATION_SCHEMA. COLUMNS where table_schema = \'marwan_group\' and COLUMN_NAME NOT IN (\"id\",\"locale\",\"updated_at\",\"created_at\",\"status\") order by TABLE_NAME;\r\n\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(94,'Multi cursor full control methodology\r\nI can for example copy all routes names and put them in class of each link without moving in cursors between different ordered lines of content It is reall a magic However It has a condtion which is:\r\nCopied cursors must equal number of cursors where I will paste\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(95,'Find file methodology \r\n1-	go to any family file ex: if searching for model got to any model\r\n2-	choose the first file in family folder\r\n3-	click the first letter of the file you are searching for and it will go theough them one by one until reach the one you are searching for \r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(96,'How to remove publi form an uploaded laravel project\r\nCrate .htaccess file and put it on root and add this content to it\r\n<IfModule mod_rewrite.c>\r\n    <IfModule mod_negotiation.c>\r\n        Options -MultiViews -Indexes\r\n    </IfModule>\r\n\r\n    RewriteEngine On\r\n\r\n    RewriteCond %{REQUEST_URI} !^/public/\r\n    RewriteRule ^(.*)$ /public/$1 [L,QSA]\r\n\r\n    # Handle Authorization Header\r\n    RewriteCond %{HTTP:Authorization} .\r\n    RewriteRule .* - [E=HTTP_AUTHORIZATION:%{HTTP:Authorization}]\r\n\r\n    # Redirect Trailing Slashes If Not A Folder...\r\n    RewriteCond %{REQUEST_FILENAME} !-d\r\n    RewriteCond %{REQUEST_URI} (.+)/$\r\n    RewriteRule ^ %1 [L,R=301]\r\n\r\n    # Send Requests To Front Controller...\r\n    RewriteCond %{REQUEST_FILENAME} !-d\r\n    RewriteCond %{REQUEST_FILENAME} !-f\r\n    RewriteRule ^ index.php [L]\r\n</IfModule>\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(97,'Automation website\r\nA website do do automatic tasks and manage projects\r\nAlways put this project in xampp htdocs to easily access it without php artisan ser\r\n\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(98,'Serve from xampp htdocs methodology\r\nAvoid php artisan ser and serve projects directly from xampp htdocs like this http://localhost/gaming-website/public/en/message\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nAngular Catalog\r\n\r\nTo get the npm version,\r\nnpm -v\r\nTo get the node version,\r\nnode -v\r\nTo get the Angular version,\r\nng v\r\nTo get the Jasmine version,\r\njasmine -v\r\nTo get the Karma version,\r\nkarma --version\r\nTo install Angular CLI,\r\nnpm install @angular/cli -g\r\nnpm install @angular/cli\r\nTo install the next version of Angular CLI,\r\nnpm install @angular/cli@next\r\nTo get help in the terminal,\r\nng help\r\nTo create a new project in Angular,\r\nng new project-name\r\nTo skip external dependencies while creating a new project,\r\nng new project-name --skip-install\r\nTo run the Angular project,\r\nng serve (or) npm start (or) ng serve --force\r\nng s -o // to open the project after serve\r\nDry Run,\r\nng new project-name --dry-run\r\nTo create a new component in the Angular Project,\r\nng generate component component-name\r\nng g c component-name\r\nTo avoid creating a new folder while creating a new component,\r\nng generate component component-name --flat\r\nTo create a build,\r\nng build\r\nTo create a build for a specific environment,\r\nng build --prod\r\nTo run test cases,\r\nng test\r\nTo run the end-to-end test,\r\nng e2e\r\nFor Angular Documentation,\r\nng doc\r\nTo change the angular-cli.json config file,\r\nng set\r\nTo create a directive in Angular,\r\nng generate directive directive-name\r\nng g d directive-name\r\nTo create a service in Angular,\r\nng generate service service-name\r\nng g s service-name\r\nTo create a class,\r\nng generate class class-name\r\nng g cl class-name\r\nTo create an interface,\r\nng generate interface interface-name\r\nng g i interface-name\r\nTo create a pipe,\r\nng generate pipe pipe-name\r\nng g p pipe-name\r\nTo create enum,\r\nng generate enum enum-name\r\nng g e enum-name\r\nTo create a module,\r\nng generate module module-name\r\nng g m module-name\r\nTo create a spec file for the module,\r\nng g m module-name --spec true -d\r\nTo create a module with routing,\r\nng g m module-name --routing\r\nTo create a guard to the route,\r\nng g guard guard-name\r\nTo remove node_modules,\r\nrm -rf node_modules\r\nTo uninstall Angular CLI,\r\nnpm uninstall --save-dev @angular/cli\r\nnpm uninstall -g angular-cli @angular/cli\r\nTo install the latest version of Angular CLI,\r\nnpm install --save-dev @angular/cli@latest\r\nTo update Angular CLI,\r\nng update @angular/cli\r\nng update @angular/core\r\nTo clean cache,\r\nnpm cache clean\r\nTo install TypeScript latest version,\r\nnpm install -g typescript@latest\r\nTo install Jasmine/Karma latest version,\r\nnpm install -g karma-jasmine@latest\r\nTo install TypeScript specific version,\r\nnpm install typescript@version-number\r\nTo install Jasmine specific version,\r\nnpm install -g jasmine@version-number\r\nTo install Karma specific version,\r\nnpm install -g karma@version-number\r\nTo run server json\r\nnpm run json-run db.json\r\nTo install bootstrap v5\r\nnpm install –save bootstrap@5 \r\n--force or --legacy-peer-deps in case of unable to resolve dependency tree Error\r\nAdd app-routing module\r\nng generate module app-routing --flat --module=app \r\nAdd ngx spinner\r\nnpm i ngx-spinner\r\nInstall ngx spinner\r\nnpm install ngx-spinner --save\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(99,'Angular packages\r\nhttps://www.positronx.io/free-angular-tutorials/ //Very important\r\nhttps://www.positronx.io/laravel-angular-token-based-authentication-with-jwt/\r\nhttps://www.positronx.io/laravel-jwt-authentication-tutorial-user-login-signup-api/\r\nIf you send the Accept header as application/json this will cause the Exception Handler to return JSON when handling the Unauthorized Exception	\r\nhttps://www.positronx.io/angular-internationalization-i18n-with-ngx-translate-tutorial/\r\nhttps://github.com/gilsdav/ngx-translate-router //localization\r\nhttps://www.youtube.com/@Kazanova22/videos //ITI Angulara and other courses\r\nhttps://www.positronx.io/how-to-integrate-owl-carousel-2-in-angular/\r\nhttps://www.learmoreseekmore.com/2022/06/angular-14-crud-example.html\r\nhttps://www.positronx.io/how-to-create-server-side-pagination-in-angular-app/\r\nhttps://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.0/components/\r\nhttps://napster2210.github.io/ngx-spinner/\r\nhttps://www.npmjs.com/package/ngx-spinner\r\nhttps://angular.io/guide/inputs-outputs\r\n//install font awesome in angular\r\nhttps://michalsnik.github.io/aos/\r\nhttps://www.npmjs.com/package/ngx-spinner\r\nhttps://animate.style/\r\nhttps://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/position //css guide\r\n//get current route\r\nhttps://stackoverflow.com/questions/34597835/how-to-get-current-route\r\n//sliders in different programming languages\r\nhttps://keen-slider.io/\r\nnpm i @fortawesome/fontawesome-free\r\n\"node_modules/@fortawesome/fontawesome-free/css/all.min.css\",\r\n\"node_modules/@fortawesome/fontawesome-free/js/all.min.js\",\r\nTo set default locale without localstorage to avoid changing current lang on reloading\r\nhttps://stackoverflow.com/questions/61010958/change-default-locale-in-angular\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(100,'Angular Lifecycle hooks\r\nngOnChanges: Called after a bound input (@input) property changes\r\nngOnInit: Called once the component is initialized (after constructor directly)\r\nngDoCheck: Called during every change detection run\r\nngAfterContentInit: Called after content (ng-content) has projected into view\r\nngAfterContentChecked: Called every time the projected content has been checked\r\nngAfterViewInit: Called after the components view (and child views) has been initialized\r\nngAfterViewChecked: Called every time the view (and child views) have been checked \r\nngOnDestroy: Called once the component is about to be destroyed\r\nNote: check them by console.log()\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(101,'Try\r\nngxspinner\r\nInstall bootstrap \r\nAnimate.css \r\nAos //animate on scroll\r\nallmediatrackby for loop\r\nProperty binding for attrbutes we add attrbute . before attrbilute name \r\n[attr.disabled]\r\nAngular material\r\nbudgets (warnings)\r\n** in routing to go for 404 page on error\r\n{ path: \'**\', component: NotFoundComponent },\r\nSafe pipe  dom sainitizer for empeddig \r\nAngular animation inout trigers\r\nbox shadow css generator\r\nColor site //to help in design colors\r\nGoogle fonts\r\nFontawsome cdn to use fontawesome in angular\r\nQuerySelector to reach elements in index\r\nngxlightbox\r\nngx pagination\r\n@input\r\n@output\r\nodd and even in css\r\n\r\n','2024-02-09 01:45:48','2024-02-09 01:45:48',1),(102,'Angular notes\r\n1-Variables that should be affected by many functions in different components must be put in a service\r\n2-we can access